('alict_00236', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'Which of the following statements about logic gates is true according to digital logic theory?', '["The output of a NOR gate is high only when at least one input is high. NOR oajdrhl", "NAND and NOR gates are considered universal gates because they can replicate only basic gates like AND OR. NAND NOR oajdri", "The exclusive NOR (XNOR) gate gives a high output when the number of high inputs is odd", "A universal gate is a gate type from which all other standard gates can be constructed", "An XOR gate outputs high only when all inputs are high XOR oajdrhla"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Option 1: A NOR gate gives a low (0) output if any of the inputs are high. The output is high only when all inputs are low. wvq Option 2: NAND and NOR gates are considered universal because they can be used to replicate all other basic gates', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 2027, 236, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00237', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'What will be the output of the above logic circuit scenario?', '["((P.Q) \u2295 Q) + ((P+Q) \u2295 P)", "((P.Q) \u2295 P) . ((P+Q) \u2295 Q)", "((P.Q) \u2295 P) + ((P+Q) \u2295 Q)", "((P.Q) \u2295 Q) + ((P.Q) \u2295 P)", "((P.Q) \u2295 P) + ((P .Q) \u2295 Q)"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Answer 3, the first AND gate will give us (P.Q) and then this is gone through an XOR gate with P input this will result in ((P', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 2027, 237, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00238', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'Choose the false statement about K-maps K-maps', '["K-maps are first introduced by Maurice Karnaugh to simplify Boolean algebra easily", "K-maps are a different way of visualising a truth table. ldfkda", "The same K-map can be written in multiple ways. tlu ldfkda", "A 3-input truth table can be mapped in 6 different ways in K-maps. 3ys", "K-maps should always obey the Grey code. ldfkda"]'::jsonb, 1, 'K-maps were introduced by Maurice but initially they weren''t used for the purpose of simplifying Boolean laws. ldfkda', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 2027, 238, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00239', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'Select the correct statement', '["SRAMs are used in cache and register memories", "SRAM synchronizes itself with the computer''s system clock. SRAM", "RAM and magnetic tapes utilize random memory access method. RAM", "SRAMs tend to offer large storage capacities. SRAM", "Because of the higher DRAMs are more expensive than SRAMs. SRAM g DRAM"]'::jsonb, 1, 'True. SRAMs are commonly used in cache memories and register files in computer systems. They are preferred for these applications because they offer fast access times and do not require refreshing like DRAMs. SRAMs fuka 2) False', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 2027, 239, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00240', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'What would be the result if the following Boolean expression is simplified?', '["P\u0305", "Q\u0305", "PQ\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305", "P\u0305Q\u0305", "(P\u0305 + Q\u0305)"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Correct answer: "P̅Q̅". This follows from evaluating the given Boolean expression / logic circuit using standard gate truth tables and Boolean algebra rules.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 2027, 240, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00241', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'What is the incorrect statement about Flip - Flop?', '["R - S (Set Reset) flip flop is the simplest flip flop from all and the easiest to understand. R - S (Set Reset)", "Flip flops can also be considered as the most basic idea of a RAM", "One form of a flip flop acts exactly like the power switch on a computer", "The two inputs are called the Set and Reset inputs", "Flip flop can be made simply by cross coupling two inverting gates either AND or gates"]'::jsonb, 5, '• Flip-flop Construction Flip-flops are typically constructed using logic gates such as NAND or NOR not simply AND or gates', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 2027, 241, '2027 Quiz Series'),
