('alict_00254', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'The following expression is derived from the instances of True in a truth table. What is the standard POS expression that can be obtained by the False instances of that truth table?', '["(A + B + C)(A + B + C\u0305)(A\u0305 + B\u0305 + C)", "(A + B\u0305 + C\u0305)(A\u0305 + B + C\u0305)", "(A + B + C)(A + B + C\u0305)(A + B\u0305 + C)(A\u0305 + B + C)(A\u0305 + B\u0305 + C)(A\u0305 + B\u0305 + C\u0305)", "(A\u0305 + B\u0305 + C)(A\u0305 + B + C\u0305)(A\u0305 + B + C)(A + B + C\u0305)(A + B + C)(A\u0305 + B\u0305 + C\u0305)", "(A\u0305 + B + C)(A + B\u0305 + C)"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The given Boolean expression must first be trivialized. = AB + C(AC + BB)̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅ = AB + C̅ + (AC + BB)̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅ De Morgan''s Law = AB + C̅ + (AC̅̅̅̅. BB̅̅̅̅) De Morgan''s Law = AB + C̅ + (AC̅̅̅̅', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 2027, 254, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00255', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'What is a primary characteristic of sequential circuits compared to combinational circuits?', '["They do not use any memory elements", "Their output depends only on current inputs", "Their output depends on the current inputs and past history", "They are faster than combinational circuits", "They require fewer components"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The explanatory table for the above question is as follows. Aspect Combinational Circuit Sequential Circuit Definition Output depends only on the current input. Output depends on both current input and past input (stored states)', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 2027, 255, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00256', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'What is the Boolean expression can be obtain from the below logic circuit?', '["1", "0", "A", "(A + B)A\u0305", "(A\u0305 + B)(A. B)"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Let''s further simplified Boolean expression obtained by above logical circuit using Boolean laws. F = (AB̅̅̅̅). (A̅ + (AB))̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅ F = AB̿̿̿̿ + (A̅ + AB̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅) De morgan''s law F = AB + (A̅ + AB̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅) Double complement law F = AB + (A̿', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 2027, 256, '2027 Quiz Series'),
