('alict_00262', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'Which of the following best describes the operation of a sequential circuit?', '["The output depends solely on the current inputs", "The output depends on the past and current inputs only if a counter is used", "The output depends on the current state of memory and current inputs", "The circuit resets automatically after each output is generated", "The circuit produces random outputs based on pre-defined probabilities"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: Incorrect. This describes a combinational not a sequential circuit. In a sequential the output also depends on the memory (past states). Option 2: Incorrect. A counter is just one type of sequential circuit', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 2027, 262, '2027 Quiz Series'),
