('alict_00488', 12, 'General ICT', 'What does Search Engine Optimization (SEO) aim to do?', '["Increase download speed of websites", "Provide antivirus protection", "Improve the visibility of a website in search engines", "Enable user authentication", "Protect websites from hackers"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Search Engine Optimization (SEO) is the process of optimizing a website to rank higher on search engine results pages (like Google or Bing), making it more visible to users searching for related terms. jeks&', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 488, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00489', 12, 'General ICT', 'A shopping website allows users to enter prices but mistakenly accepts negative values. What validation method should be added?', '["Format check", "Range check", "Presence check", "Verification check", "Consistency check"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Ensures the value falls within an acceptable range (price must be greater than or equal to zero). Correct choice because the website should reject negative values. w.h Option 1: Checks if the input follows a specific such as a date being in DD containing @', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 489, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00490', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the following best describes fourth-generation computers?', '["Used vacuum tubes", "Used integrated circuits", "Used microprocessors", "Used punch cards", "Operated using mechanical switches"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Analysis of Each 1) Used vacuum tubes - Incorrect • Vacuum tubes were used in first-generation computers (1940 - 1956). 2) Used integrated circuits - Incorrect • Integrated Circuits (ICs) were a key technology in third-generation computers (1964-1971)', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 490, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00491', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the following statements best describes a key difference between and CRT display technologies?', '["LCD monitors use cathode ray unlike CRT which uses liquid crystals. LCD fudksgr", "CRT displays consume less power than both LCD and LED technologies due to efficient tube design", "LED displays are simply that use light-emitting diodes for backlighting instead of cold cathode tubes. LED", "LCD displays emit light directly from the screen whereas CRT and LED use internal bulbs. LCD", "All three technologies use pixel-based digital rendering and flat panel structures"]'::jsonb, 3, 'A monitor is an essential output device that displays information from a computer in visual such as and videos. It allows users to interact with the system by showing what''s happening in real time', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 491, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00492', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the following statements about disk allocation methods is incorrect?', '["In contiguous each file occupies a set of consecutive blocks on the disk. hdno", "Linked allocation avoids external fragmentation by using pointers in each block", "Indexed allocation avoids both internal and external fragmentation", "Linked allocation allows direct access to any block in constant time", "Contiguous allocation suffers from difficulty in file growth due to fixed space. bvla"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Option 1: In contiguous all the blocks of a file are stored sequentially on the disk. This makes accessing the file very fast since the system can calculate the location of any block using simple arithmetic', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 492, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00493', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which statement best explains the difference between impact and non-impact printers?', '["Impact printers strike the paper with pins or hammers through an ink while non-impact printers print without touching the using methods like lasers or ink jets", "Non-impact printers are louder and slower than impact especially when printing lots of pages", "Impact printers are better for printing detailed images and graphics", "Non-impact printers print by hitting the paper with mechanical parts like pins or hammers", "Impact printers cannot print on multi-copy forms like carbon paper"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Printers are essential output devices that convert digital information from computers into physical hard typically on paper. They come in two main impact printers and non-impact printers. Explanation of each option 1: This is correct', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 493, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00494', 12, 'General ICT', 'Which of the following is NOT a feature of Indexed Allocation?', '["Eliminates external fragmentation", "Direct access to blocks is possible fldgia(blocks)", "Each block contains a pointer to the next fldgilu(block)", "File ends at a null pointer", "Uses an index block to manage pointers"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Indexed Allocation is a file allocation method used by file systems to manage files on disk. fjka Option 1: Since blocks can be scattered anywhere on the there''s no need to allocate them contiguously. it avoids external fragmentation', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 494, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00495', 12, 'General ICT', '100.7510 + 32.38 equant for?', '["A only. A", "B only. B", "A and C only. A C", "B and C only. B C", "None of the above"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Correct answer: "None of the above".', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 495, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00496', 12, 'General ICT', 'A system has a 24-bit virtual address and a page size of 4 KB. Based on this how many bits are used for the page offset?', '["10", "12", "154", "16", "8"]'::jsonb, 2, 'A virtual address is divided into two parts 1) Page number (which page) 2) Page offset (where in that page) What is the page offset The page offset is the number of bits used to specify the location within a page', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 496, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00497', 12, 'General ICT', 'NOT operation of the value 1100012 will 1100012 w.fha NOT fufyhqu', '["1110102", "0101012", "0001102", "11110102", "0011102"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Explanation of the NOT Operation on Binary Numbers The NOT also known as bitwise NOT or binary is a fundamental operation in binary logic. This operation works by inverting each bit of a binary number. In other each 1 in the binary number becomes a 0, and each 0 becomes a 1', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 497, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00498', 12, 'General ICT', 'In a system with a 25-bit virtual address space and a page size of 4 how many pages are there in the virtual address space?', '["29", "211", "213", "215", "217"]'::jsonb, 3, 'In a computer the virtual address space defines how much memory a process can access. If the virtual address space is 25 it means the system can generate 225 unique addresses. Since each address points to 1 the total virtual memory available is 225 bytes', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'General ICT', 2027, 498, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00499', 11, 'ICT & Society, Security, E-commerce', 'What is the role of Big Data analysis in modern ICT systems?', '["Managing small-scale data operations", "Analyzing structured and unstructured data for insights", "Reducing the complexity of manual calculations", "Limiting the usage of cloud computing services", "Replacing traditional databases with hierarchical models"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Big Data analysis involves processing and analyzing large volumes of structured and unstructured data to gain valuable identify and support decision -making', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'ICT & Society, Security, E-commerce', 2027, 499, '2027 Quiz Series'),
