('alict_00570', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'In computers assist in verifying medication information like drug labels and expiry dates. Which system is responsible for this?', '["Diagnostic System", "Patient Monitoring System", "Lab-Diagnostic System", "Pharmacy Information System", "Surgical Support System"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Diagnostic System This system assists in diagnosing medical conditions through data such as lab and patient history. It does not typically handle medication verification. u', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 570, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00571', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the following statements about data and information is incorrect?', '["Data is always meaningful and directly just like information", "Data consists of raw or whereas information is meaningful and organized data", "Data must be processed through or computation to become useful information", "The accuracy and reliability of information depend on the quality of the data used to generate it", "Information helps in whereas raw data alone may not be directly useful"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Option 1: Incorrect. Data is raw and meaning it may not always be meaningful or directly useful. It becomes useful only after processing. Option 2: Correct. Data is while information is processed and meaningful. Option 3: Correct', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 571, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00572', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the following is an advanced application of ICT (Information and Communication Technology) in agriculture that optimizes resource allocation?', '["Manually controlling irrigation times based on personal judgment", "Using simple soil testing kits for nutrient analysis", "Implementing machine learning models for predicting crop diseases fnda. frda", "Relying on historical yield data without real-time analysis", "Maintaining traditional farm equipment without sensors"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Machine learning (ML) is an advanced application of ICT in agriculture that significantly enhances decision-making by leveraging data-driven insights', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 572, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00573', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the following is a key characteristic of Big Data?', '["It only deals with structured data. th", "Traditional databases are sufficient for handling it", "It requires advanced tools for storage and analysis", "It does not need high-speed processing. thg", "Small-scale storage methods can handle Big Data efficiently. l%u uyd"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: This is incorrect. Big Data deals with all types of data semi and unstructured). It can include data from social sensor and much not just structured data. fndfyda foa Option 2: This is incorrect', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 573, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00574', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'What is a key benefit of ICT in education?', '["Increased physical activity", "Quick access to information", "Limited communication options", "Decreased use of technology", "Higher cost of learning"]'::jsonb, 2, 'ICT provides students and educators with fast and convenient access to vast such as research online and educational videos. ICT u', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 574, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00575', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'A retail company uses big data analytics to predict customer purchasing patterns. Which of the following is an example of how big data could help the company?', '["Offering the same discounts to all customers. tlu", "Predicting which a customer might buy next", "Storing customer data in a local spreadsheet", "Sending random promotional emails to customers", "Limiting stock to avoid overproduction entirely"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: This does not utilize big data analytics as it treats all customers equally without personalizing offers based on purchasing behavior', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 575, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00576', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the following is a limitation of the V on Neumann architecture?', '["It supports multi-threading for parallel task execution. th", "It requires separate memory for instructions and data. Wmfoia", "The V on Neumann bottleneck can lead to performance issues. V on Neumann bottleneck", "It uses a non-linear memory access pattern. th", "It has limited support for complex mathematical operations"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The V on Neumann architecture is a computer design model that uses a single memory for both instructions and data. While it is widely it has a key limitation known as the V on Neumann which can slow down performance due to limited data transfer between the CPU and memory', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 576, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00577', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'One of the fundamental principles of the V on Neumann architecture fjdka kshquka', '["Utilizing multiple processing units for parallel execution", "Storing both instructions and data in separate memory locations. Wmfoia", "Fetching and executing instructions sequentially from memory", "Employing a complex control unit for pipelined instruction processing", "Implementing a non-uniform memory access scheme"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The Von Neumann architecture is characterized by the use of a single address space for both instructions and data. This means that the CPU fetches instructions and data from the same memory unit', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 577, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00578', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'What is the purpose of a "file backup" in file management?', '["To create a duplicate of a file", "To restore lost files", "To protect against data loss", "All of the above", "None of the above"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Let''s consider each option one by one. Option 1: This is correct because a backup involves making a copy of the original file to ensure that data is available even if the original file is lost or corrupted', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 578, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00579', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'What is the name given to data consisting of descriptive characteristics that cannot be measured separately?', '["Quantitative data", "Qualitative data", "Discrete data", "Spatial data", "Structured data"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Quantitative Data This type of data is numerical and can be measured and counted. It includes data such as and which can be represented using numbers and often subjected to statistical analysis', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 579, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00580', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the following is an example of real-time processing?', '["Payroll calculation", "Billing system", "Automatic production line", "Data backup", "Batch data entry"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: This process typically happens such as weekly or and does not require immediate results after each data entry. it is not an example of real-time processing', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 580, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00581', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the following statements is false regarding QR codes?', '["QR code stands for Quick Recognition code. QR", "Some QR codes can track scanning information such as number of location etc. iuyr QR", "A type of two-dimensional matrix code", "Stores data both horizontally and vertically", "Has 3 squares allowing the scanning device to determine the orientation"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Option 1: This statement is false. The acronym "QR" in QR code stands for "Quick Response" not "Quick Recognition" code. Recognition" Option 2: It is true that certain QR codes can be encoded to track various types of scanning information', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 581, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00582', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'The age limit is represented from 19 to 22 when students are registered for university entrance via the website. Which of the following data validation method is most appropriate for this situation?', '["Type check", "Range check", "Numeric check", "Format check", "Presence check"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: The type check ensures that the data entered is of the correct data type. For it verifies that the input is numeric rather than text. While it confirms that the data is of a certain type (like numbers), it does not validate whether the numeric value falls within a specified range', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 582, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00583', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the following is a disadvantage of disk defragmentation?', '["Increased disk speed after defragmentation", "Requires a lot of system resources while running", "Improves file organization on the disk", "Can recover lost data", "Helps prevent disk wear and tear"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Disk defragmentation consumes a large amount of system resources such as CPU disk and memory while it is running. Because of the system can become and unresponsive during the especially on low-end computers', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 583, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00584', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the following is NOT a factor which affects the quality of information?', '["File size", "Completeness", "Level of details", "Age of the audience", "Accuracy"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The quality of information is typically assessed based on various factors that determine how and relevant the information is for decision-making. These factors include • Completeness Ensures all necessary information is included', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 584, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00585', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the following is a good example of real-time processing?', '["Library book check-out system", "Automated stock market trading system", "Daily website traffic analytics", "Monthly sales report generation", "Yearly tax report preparation"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Real-time processing refers to systems that respond immediately to input and produce instant results. Let''s review each option. Option 1: This system processes data instantly when a book is checked out. it doesn''t require the strict timing that real-time processing demands', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 585, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00586', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the following statement', '["Used to store data on computers", "Used to transmitting data in networks", "Used for low level programming", "Used in microcontrollers", "All of the above"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Some uses of binary number system is as follows. - Processing data on computers - Storing data on computers - Transmitting data in networks - Encryption of data - Low level programming - For microcontrollers 3', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 586, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00587', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Data Creation ,................... , Removal of obsolete ,..................... , .sh of the following is suitable for the above blank?', '["Data storing", "Data Management", "Data presenting", "Data gathering", "Data editing"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Data management involves and maintaining data effectively throughout its lifecycle', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 587, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00588', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'In which processing method is data handled in groups?', '["Real-time processing", "Interactive processing", "Batch processing", "Continuous processing", "Deferred processing"]'::jsonb, 3, 'In Batch data is handled in meaning that multiple data entries or transactions are collected over a period of time and processed together in one go. This method is efficient for large volumes of data that don''t need immediate processing', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 588, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00589', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the followings are steps in data processing?', '["Data and decryption", "Data and reporting", "Data output and", "Data and decompression", "Data and execution"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Fundamental Steps in Data • Data Collection Gathering raw data from various sources. wuq • Data Validation Ensuring that the data is and reliable', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 589, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00590', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'What is the primary purpose of a screen iq', '["To increase the brightness of the screen", "To reduce eye strain during prolonged periods of inactivity", "To display advertisements on the screen", "To improve the performance of the computer''s graphics card. .%e*sla", "To encrypt sensitive information on the screen"]'::jsonb, 2, '• Statement A screen saver does not increase the brightness of the screen. In some screen savers dim the screen to reduce brightness and save energy. ;sr iq • Statement The traditional purpose of a screen saver is not to display advertisements', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 590, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00591', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'What is the primary purpose of using multiplexers in digital circuits?', '["To store multiple bits of data simultaneously", "To perform arithmetic operations like addition and subtraction", "To select one input from multiple inputs and forward it to the output. nyq", "To generate clock signals for synchronizing the circuit", "To convert digital signals into analog signals"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The primary purpose of using multiplexers (MUX) in digital circuits is to select one input from multiple inputs and forward it to the output. A multiplexer acts like a choosing one of several data inputs and sending it to the output line based on the control signals', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 591, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00592', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'What is the Golden Rule of Information in information security and data management?', '["Information should be encrypted before transmission", "The value of information decreases with time", "Data must be backed up regularly to prevent loss", "Information should be accessible to everyone in the organization", "Use strong passwords for all accounts containing sensitive information"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The Golden Rule of Information emphasizes that information is most valuable when it is timely-as time its usefulness and relevance often declines. - Options 1, 3, and 5 are good security practices but do not describe the golden rule', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 592, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00593', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'In which memory segment does the OS store temporary such as function parameters and return addresses?', '["Stack Segment", "Code Segment", "Data Segment", "Heap Segment", "Instruction Segment"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Stack Segment According to this it''s true. The stack segment is used to store temporary data such as function local and return addresses during function calls and execution. return addresses jeks 2) Code Segment According to this it''s false', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 593, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00594', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the following is NOT a key characteristic of modern flash memory technology?', '["Ability to be electrically erased and reprogrammed", "Non-volatile data storage without power", "Faster read", "Integrated fingerprint sensor for enhanced security", "Scalable storage capacity in a compact form factor"]'::jsonb, 4, '• Option 1: This is a fundamental characteristic of flash memory. Unlike some other types of flash memory can be electrically erased and which allows for its data to be updated or changed', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 594, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00595', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'What is the incorrect statement regarding the manual and computerized data input methods?', '["accuracy is high", "faster data input", "cost effectiveness", "minimal requirements of data verification", "compulsory to verify all the data inserted using computerized method"]'::jsonb, 5, '2025/09/03 Information and Communication Technology The statement "compulsory to verify all the data inserted using a computerized method" is incorrect regarding manual and computerized data input methods', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 595, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00596', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the following is the correct order of the data processing steps?', '["Data output \u2192 Data validation \u2192 Data storage \u2192 Data gathering \u2192 Data \u2192 \u2192 \u2192", "Data gathering \u2192 Data processing \u2192 Data validation \u2192 Data output \u2192 Data", "Data gathering \u2192 Data validation \u2192 Data processing \u2192 Data output \u2192 Data", "Data processing \u2192 Data output \u2192 Data storage \u2192 Data gathering \u2192 Data \u2192 \u2192 \u2192", "Data validation \u2192 Data gathering \u2192 Data storage \u2192 Data processing \u2192 Data \u2192"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "Data gathering → Data validation → Data processing → Data output → Data". This follows from the standard definitions of data, information, and ICT processing concepts.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 596, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00597', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'In an abstract model of an information what is the role of the processing stage?', '["To generate useful information without any input", "To control the flow of data into subsystems. Wm", "To apply instructions to input data to produce information", "To combine input and output for system optimization", "To act as a storage unit for data only"]'::jsonb, 3, 'In an abstract model of an information the processing stage plays a crucial role in converting input data into meaningful information. This is achieved by applying specific or algorithms to the input data', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 597, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00598', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'In the indexed allocation how is file data stored on the disk?', '["In contiguous blocks of memory", "Through an index block that contains pointers to all data blocks", "In linked lists where each block points to the next block", "By storing the entire file in a single block", "With no need for additional metadata"]'::jsonb, 2, 'In the indexed allocation each file has an index block that stores pointers to the actual blocks where the file data is stored on the disk. This method allows the data blocks to be enabling better space utilization. lr bv', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 2027, 598, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00599', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Yashodhara says that when a student enters the marks obtained in three A-level subjects in a program that displays the average of the numbers in the column that displays the average should be decimal numbers (Real). Which of these data validity tests is called?', '["Type check", "Availability check", "Range check (mrdi", "Data check", "Real-time data processing"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Type check ensures that the entered data is of the correct data type. In this scenario − The program expects real numbers (decimal values) as the average mark', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 599, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00600', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What is the octal value that is equivalent to decimal 10810?', '["1508", "1548", "1088", "748", "548"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Convert decimal 10810 to octal: 10810(10) = 10810(10) = 25072(8). This matches "1548".', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 600, '2027 Quiz Series')
