('alict_00665', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What is the false statement about sign-magnitude?', '["Used to represent positive and negative numbers in the computer. Ok", "Used 1 to represent the negative numbers and 0 to positive numbers as the first bit. 1 Ok 0", "Except for the first bit other bits are used to represent the absolute value. w.h", "To get the sign-magnitude value of a negative we should get the binary value of it and inverse it", "Conversions between positive and negative numbers are simple. Ok"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Option 1: This is correct. Sign magnitude is a method used in computers to represent both positive and negative numbers. Option 2: This is correct. The first bit (most significant bit) is the sign where 1 represents a negative number and 0 represents a positive number', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 665, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00666', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'The ASCII representation of some words as follows. jpk ASCII 01000001 01110101 01110010 01101111 01110010 01100001 meat 01101101 01100101 01100001 01110100 Pipeline 01010000 01101001 01110000 01100101 01101100 01101001 01101110 01100101 hey VI 01101000 01100101 01111001 00100000 01010110 01001001 What is the ASCII representation of "Alpha', '["01000001 01101100 01110000 01101000 01100001 00100000 01010111 01100001 01101101 01010000", "01000001 01101100 01110000 01101000 01100001 00100000 01010110 01101001 01101101 01010000", "01000001 01101101 01110000 01101000 01100001 00100000 01010110 01100001 01101101 01010001", "01000001 01101100 01110000 01101000 01100010 00100000 01010110 01100001 01101101 01010000", "01000001 01101100 01110000 01101000 01100001 00100000 01010110 01100001 01101101 01010000"]'::jsonb, 5, 'The ASCII representation of "Alpha must be determined by converting each character into its corresponding 8-bit binary ASCII value. "Alpha ASCII w', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 666, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00667', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'According to the ASCII encoding the decimal representation of A is 65, and the decimal representation of z is 122. What is the binary representation of the word in ASCII?', '["01100100 01010101 00110001 01001100 01101111", "01100100 01010101 01100101 01001100 01101111", "01100100 01010101 01100101 01001100 00110010", "01100100 01010101 01100101 00110011 01101111", "01100100 00110100 01100101 01001100 01101111"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Capital letters When A = 6510, U = 8510 = 10101012 = ASCII 01010101 L = 7610 = 10011002 = ASCII 01001100 Simple letters When z = 12210, d = 10010 = 11001002 ASCII 01100100 e = 10110 = 11001012 ASCII 01100101 o = 11110 = 11011112 ASCII 01101111 2 111 2 55 - 1 2 27 - 1 2 13 - 1 2 6 - 1 2 3 - 0 2 1 - 1', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 667, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00668', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Which of the following is the correct binary representation of -45 using the 8-bit 2''s complement method?', '["001011012", "110100112", "101100112", "110110112", "101011012"]'::jsonb, 2, 'convert 45 to Binary (positive). As we represent the 2''s complement value in 8 bits we should add 0s before the whole value. wms 8 lska foflys w.h 4510 = 001011012 To take the 2''s first we should invert the bits and get the 1''s complement', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 668, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00669', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What is the result when the hexadecimal number 1F.A is converted to decimal?', '["31.625", "30.8125", "32.125", "33.5", "31.75"]'::jsonb, 1, 'To convert 1F.A16 into convert the integer part (1F) and the fractional part (A) into decimal. 1F.A16 1F.A16 1 F (15) . A (10) 161 160 . 16-1 16 × 1 × 15 . 0.0625 × 10 16 + 15 + 0.625 31.62510', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 669, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00670', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Which of the following is a limitation of BCD when used for arithmetic operations?', '["BCD cannot represent negative numbers. BCD", "BCD arithmetic requires additional hardware for operations like addition and subtraction. BCD wxl", "BCD does not support fractional numbers. BCD Nd", "BCD encoding causes rounding errors for decimal calculations. BCD", "BCD cannot be used for digital display systems"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: Incorrect. BCD can represent negative numbers by using sign representation techniques sign - magnitude representation). ix{d Option 2: Correct', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 670, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00671', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'A number X is represented as 2F.AC16 in hexadecimal. What is its decimal equivalent?', '["47.671875", "46.671875", "45.8125", "47.8125", "46.8125"]'::jsonb, 1, 'To convert 2F.AC16 into convert the integer part (2F) and the fractional part (AC) into decimal. 2F.AC16 2F.AC16 2 F (15) . A (10) C (12) 161 160 . 16-1 16-2 16 × 2 1 × 15 . 0.0625 × 10 0.00390625 × 12 32 15 . 0.625 0.046875 32 + 15 + 0.626 + 0.046875 47.67187510', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 671, '2027 Quiz Series'),
