('alict_00674', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Which of the following is a primary advantage of Unicode over traditional character encoding standards like ASCII?', '["It uses fewer bits per resulting in smaller file sizes. th wvq", "It supports a significantly larger range of encompassing most of the world''s writing systems. th", "It is exclusively designed for English language text. th bx.%Sis", "It is limited to representing only numeric characters. th", "It is only compatible with legacy mainframe systems. th legacy mainframe"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: Incorrect. especially in its UTF-16 and UTF-32 often uses more bits per character than ASCII. UTF-8, can use the same number of bits as ASCII for standard english characters. Option 2: Correct', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 674, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00675', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'You and your friend are on a secret mission and have devised a unique way to communicate. You''ve chosen to encode your messages using 8-bit ASCII. To make decryption even more you''ve decided to insert a random 8-bit ASCII character after every two consecutive letters in your message. Tn ryia fufyhqul Tn 8-bit ASCII follgu miqj 8-bit Tn lr would be the corresponding ASCII-encoded message for this?', '["01010100 01101111 00100011 01100100 01100001 00100100 01111001 00100000 01100001 01110100 00100101 00100000 00110111 00101110 00110000 00100000 01110000 01101101 00100001 00101110", "01010100 01101111 00100011 01100100 01100001 00100100 01111001 00100000 01100001 00100011 01110100 00100000 00110111 00101110 00110000 0011 0000 00100000 00100101 01110000 01101101 00100110 00101110", "01010100 01101111 00100011 01100100 01100001 00100100 01111001 00100000 01100001 01110100 00100000 00110111 00101110 00110000 00100110 00110000 00100000 01110000 00100001 01101101 00100110 00101110", "01110100 01101111 00100011 01100100 01100001 00100100 01111001 00100000 01100001 01110100 00100000 00110111 00101110 00110000 00100000 01110000 01101101 00101110", "01110100 01101111 00100011 01100100 01100001 00100100 01111001 00100000 01100001 01010100 00100000 00110111 00101110 00110000 00100000 01110000 01101101 00101110"]'::jsonb, 1, 'As you all in 8-bit ASCII Tn okakd 8-bit ASCII • 00110000 (48₁₀) - 00111001 (57₁₀) represents 0-9 • 01000001 (65₁₀) - 01011010 (90₁₀) represents A-Z • 01100001 (97₁₀) - 01111010 (122₁₀) represents a-z Using this you can determine the next character by adding 1 to the 8-bit v', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 675, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00676', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'In the binary number what does the term "overflow" mean in computing?', '["A program takes too long to run. jevigykla", "A binary number becoming too large for the memory space assigned", "A keyboard sending too many inputs at once", "A calculation giving a result too big for the allowed number of bits. .Kkh wjir", "A variable is created but not used in the program"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Option 1: This is related to performance or not overflow. Overflow refers to numerical not execution time. Option 2: This is but it''s a bit vague. Overflow is specifically when the result of a calculation exceeds the bit limit 8-bit addition result needing 9 bits)', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 676, '2027 Quiz Series'),
