('alict_00679', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Which of the following options shows the correct BCD and binary representations of 74, respectively?', '["01001010BCD , 10010102", "01010100BCD , 11011002", "01101110BCD , 10010102", "01100100BCD , 10010012", "01110100BCD , 10010102"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Step Finding the BCD value BCD (Binary Coded Decimal) is a method for representing decimal digits in binary form. Each decimal digit is encoded as a 4-bit binary number. BCD ixLHdxlhlau Step Finding the binary value Accordingly BCD = 0111 0100BCD Binary = 10010102', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 679, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00680', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What is the smallest among the following binary operations?', '["10102 OR 11012", "10102 XOR 11012", "10102 AND 11012", "NOT (10102 OR 11012)", "NOT (10102 XOR 11012)"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Option 1: 10102 OR 11012 11112 = 1510 Option 2: 10102 XOR 11012 1112 = 710 Option 3: 10102 AND 11012 10002 = 810 Option 4: NOT (10102 OR 11012) 10102 OR 11012 NOT (11112) = 00002 = 010 Option 5: NOT (10102 XOR 11012) 10102 XOR 11012 NOT (01012) = 10102 = 1010 Comp', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 680, '2027 Quiz Series'),
