('alict_00682', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Convert the octal number 726₈ to its equivalent hexadecimal representation. 726₈ thg iudk', '["D6\u2081\u2086", "E6\u2081\u2086", "F4\u2081\u2086", "C6\u2081\u2086", "B6\u2081\u2086"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Let''s convert the octal value into hexadecimal. 7268 7 2 6 111 010 110 111010110 0001 1101 0110 1 D (13) 6 1D616', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 682, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00683', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'A digital clock uses BCD encoding to represent each digit of the current time. At one the clock displays the time The microcontroller inside reads the digits separately and converts each digit into its 4-bit binary-coded decimal (BCD) BCD lrhs'' tla fjk fjku lshjd tys 4 binary-coded decimal (BCD) lrhs. Which of the following correctly represents the full BCD encoding of the time', '["1001 0000 0100 0111", "1001 0000 0111 0100", "0000 1001 0111 0100", "0000 1001 0100 0111", "1001 0000 0110 1000"]'::jsonb, 4, 'BCD is a method of representing decimal numbers (0 -9) in binary w here each decimal digit is represented by 4 binary bits. BCD ixLHdxlhlau Digits BCD encoding (4 bits per digit) 0 = 0000 9 = 1001 4 = 0100 7 = 0111 1) DFA16 2) B7A16 3) D7A16 4) DAE16 5) ID7A16 Correct BCD sequence', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 683, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00684', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Which of the following statements about complementary number systems is true?', '["1''s complement of a binary number is found by adding 1 to it", "2''s complement is obtained by flipping all bits of a binary number", "1''s complement and 2''s complement of a number are always the same. 1 2", "2''s complement is obtained by taking the 1''s complement and adding 1 to it. 1 f.k thg 1", "1''s complement is used more often than 2''s complement for representing signed numbers"]'::jsonb, 4, 'The 1''s complement and 2''s complement are two methods for representing negative numbers in binary systems. 1''s Complement Obtained by flipping all bits (changing 0s to 1s and 1s to 0s). 2''s Complement Obtained by taking the 1''s complement and then adding 1. 1 f.k 1 la', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 684, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00685', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Select the correct answer for (-7) + (-4), using 8-bit two''s complement representation. 8 fofla', '["0000 10112", "1111 01112", "1111 01012", "0000 01012", "1111 00112"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Convert to binary 7 in binary 4 in binary Find two''s complement for negatives For -7 Invert the bits (1111 1000) and add 1 (1111 1001). For -4 Invert the bits (1111 1011) and add 1 (1111 1100)', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 685, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00686', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What is Unicode primarily used for?', '["To represent mathematical symbols only", "To represent characters from most of the world''s writing systems", "To encode only English characters bx.%Sis", "To encode graphical images", "To convert binary code to text"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: Incorrect because Unicode is not limited to just mathematical symbols. It covers a wide range of characters from various scripts. Option 2: Correct. Unicode is a universal character encoding standard that aims to represent characters from most of the world''s writing systems', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 686, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00687', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Which of the following statements is true regarding the relationship between Karnaugh Maps and Gray Code?', '["Gray code is used to arrange the cells of a K-map so that adjacent cells differ by only one bit. ldfkda", "K-map cells are always arranged in binary code order to ensure proper not Gray code order. ksis", "Gray code is used exclusively to convert binary values to decimal in K-map groupings. ldfkda", "The groupings in a K-map always follow Gray code order for correct simplification. ldfkda", "Gray code is used to minimize the number of variables in K-map grouping. ldfkda"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Gray code is a binary numeral system where two successive values differ in only one bit. This property is crucial for K-maps. Gray code In a Karnaugh the rows and columns are arranged using Gray code', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 687, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00688', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Convert 101110101101. 01112 into hexadecimal 101110101101. 01112', '["B57.716", "BA5.416", "D5.816", "BAD.716", "B55.716"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Let''s convert the binary value into hexadecimal', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 688, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00689', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'A digital system is designed to store integers in an 8 -bit sign -magnitude representation. The most significant bit (MSB) is used as the sign where 0 represents a positive number and 1 represents a negative number. The remaining 7 bits represent the magnitude of the number in binary. ixLHdxl lr ksrEmKhlska fjfiis w.h MSB 0 Ok 1 7 lrhs'' A sensor in a temperature monitoring system outputs values in 8-bit sign-magnitude format. The sensor records the following lrhs( 10010110₂. What is the decimal equivalent of this reading?', '["22", "-153", "-150", "-22", "150"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Given the 8-bit sign-magnitude number Identify the Sign Bit The most significant bit (MSB) (leftmost bit) is 1, indicating that this is a negative number. Obtain the Magnitude The remaining 7 bits (excluding the MSB) represent the magnitude', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 689, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00690', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Why is Gray code used in Karnaugh Maps?', '["It allows each cell to represent multiple minterms. th cell tllgu nyq", "It ensures only one variable changes between adjacent cells. th cell", "It minimizes the number of K-Map variables. th ldfkda", "It makes binary counting faster in digital circuits. th", "It ensures all variables change simultaneously between adjacent cells. th cells"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: Each K-Map cell represents exactly one not multiple. ldfkda Option 2: Gray code is used in K-Maps so that only one-bit (variable) changes between adjacent cells. This property is crucial for valid groupings during simplification', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 690, '2027 Quiz Series'),
