('alict_00692', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What is the one''s complement of the answer obtained by calculating 111010012 - 100111012 ?', '["101100112", "010011002", "101101002", "010011012", "110011002"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Converting the binary numbers into decimal 111010012 100111012 1 0 1 0 1 0 1 0 1 27 26 25 24 23 22 21 20 27 26 25 24 23 22 21 20 128 64 32 16 8 4 2 1 128 64 32 16 8 4 2 1 128 + 64 + 32 + 8 + 1 128 + 16 + 8 + 4 + 1 23310 15710 Calculation = 23310 - 15710 = 7610 Converting the decimal nu', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 692, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00693', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Why do computers use the binary number system instead of other number systems like decimal?', '["Binary lets computers avoid errors caused by decimals", "Binary number system is the easiest for humans to understand", "Binary system uses less electricity in all cases", "Binary system is easier to build using electronic circuits", "Binary helps software install faster on devices"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Option 1: While binary avoids some decimal rounding that''s not why it''s the chosen number system. binary has its own precision especially with floating-point numbers. ksid Option 2: humans find decimal easier because we use it in everyday life', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 693, '2027 Quiz Series'),
