('alict_00697', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'From the given 3 binary numbers (A = 0, B = 1, C in = 0) , calculate the sum and carry out using a (A = 0, B = 1, C in = 0) , (sum) iy', '["sum = 0, carryout = 0", "sum = 1, carryout = 1", "sum = 1, carryout = 0", "sum = 0, carryout = 1", "Not enough data has been provided"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Sum = A + B + Cin = 0 +1 +0 = 1 Carry out (Cout) = (A.B) + (B.Cin) + (A.Cin) = (0.1) + (1.0) + (0.0) = 0 Sum = 1 Carryout = 0', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 697, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00698', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What is the 1''s complement value equivalent to -45 in 8-bit notation?', '["001011012", "110100102", "101011012", "111010102", "000101012"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Step Represent 45 in Binary (8-bit) 2 45 2 22 -1 2 11 -0 2 5 -1 2 -1 2 1 -0 -1 4510 = 001011012 Step Find the 1''s complement To calculate the 1''s flip all the bits (change 0 to 1 and 1 to 0):', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 698, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00699', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'A digital counter uses Binary Coded Decimal (BCD) to represent each digit of the count. At a the counter displays the value 25. The internal processing unit reads each digit individually and converts it into its corresponding 4-bit BCD representation. ixLHdxl ljqkagrhla .Kkh ljqkagrh 25 w.h fjk fjku th BCD lrhs'' Which of the following options accurately represents the full BCD encoding of the displayed value 25?', '["0010 0101", "0101 0010", "0010 0011", "0001 0101", "0011 0101"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The question asks for the BCD encoding of the number 25. In each decimal digit is represented by its own 4-bit binary equivalent. m%Yakh wxl 25 BCD For the digit 2: The binary representation of 2 is 0010. wxl 2 For the digit 5: The binary representation of 5 is 0101', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 699, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00700', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'A delivery drone can move forward (positive distance) or backward (negative distance) along a straight path from its base station. The movement data is stored in an 8 -bit register using 2''s complement representation. One the drone moves -45 units from its fv%dak tys isg ud¾.hla Tiafia fyda miqmig .uka 2 lr fv%dakh tys isg -45 la lrhs'' What is the 8-bit binary representation of this movement?', '["00101101", "11001111", "00101100", "11010011", "01001011"]'::jsonb, 4, 'the question asks to get the 2''s complement of -45. we want to get the binary value of 45. -45 2 ,nd m%Yakh = 1011012 As we represent the 2''s complement value in 8 we should add 0s before the whole value. wms 8 lska 2 w', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 700, '2027 Quiz Series')
INSERT INTO public.questions (id, unit, unit_title, question_text, options, correct_option, explanation, latex_formula, trap_insight, difficulty, topic, past_paper_year, past_paper_number, series)
VALUES
('alict_00701', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What is the long name for the memory chip that stores the BIOS firmware in a computer?', '["Complementary Matrix Octal Semiconductor", "Complementary Metal Oxide Semiconductor", "Controllable Metal Octal Sensors", "Controllable Matrix Oxide Semiconductor", "Collector Metal Oxide Selector"]'::jsonb, 2, 'CMOS is a technology used in the manufacturing of integrated including the memory chip that stores the BIOS (Basic Input CMOS is often used to refer to the small amount of volatile memory that stores the BIOS firmware settings', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 701, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00702', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What is the decimal equivalent of the hexadecimal number A816 ?', '["170", "160", "168", "175", "157"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "168". This follows from converting/calculating the given number(s) using standard place-value (base) arithmetic.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 702, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00703', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Which of the following statements is true about the EBCDIC encoding system?', '["EBCDIC is a 7-bit character encoding scheme. EBCDIC", "EBCDIC stands for Extended Binary Coded Decimal Interchange Code. EBCDIC", "EBCDIC is primarily used in modern web development for encoding. EBCDIC", "EBCDIC is an 8-bit character encoding scheme used primarily in IBM mainframes. EBCDIC", "EBCDIC supports a maximum of 128 characters. EBCDIC"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Option 1: This statement is incorrect. EBCDIC is an 8-bit encoding not 7-bit (ASCII uses a 7-bit system). Option 2: This is a true but not the best answer here since it''s not the focus of the question. Option 3: This is incorrect', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 703, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00704', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'A short story contains 256 including spaces and punctuation. If each character is encoded using the ASCII standard along with one extra parity bit for error what is the total number of bits required to store this short story?', '["256", "256 \u00d7 7", "256 \u00d7 8", "256 \u00d7 9", "256 / 8"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The ASCII standard typically uses 7 bits to represent each character. This allows for different characters. ASCII 2025/05/03 Information and Communication Technology The question states that an additional parity bit is used for each character', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 704, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00705', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'While examining the memory of a vintage gaming you encounter the hexadecimal value "B3". Convert this hexadecimal number to its binary divide the binary into two 4-bit and then determine the decimal equivalent of the second group', '["3", "11", "12", "13", "19"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Convert the hexadecimal number "B3" to binary. "B3" B3 B (11) 3 23 22 21 20 23 22 21 20 8 4 2 1 8 4 2 1 0 1 0 1 1st group 2nd group Determine the decimal equivalent of the second group. fojk 0 1 23 22 21 20 - - 2 1 2 + 1 3', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 705, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00706', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What is the range of values that can be represented by 8-bit 2''s complement form?', '["-128 to 127", "-128 to 128", "-127 to 127", "-127 to 128", "-256 to 256"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "-128 to 127". This follows from converting/calculating the given number(s) using standard place-value (base) arithmetic.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 706, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00707', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Consider the following octal ,decimal ,binary and hexa decimal', '["Both B and D are Equal", "D is the largest number", "Both A and C are Equal", "Both", "and"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "Both A and C are Equal". This follows from converting/calculating the given number(s) using standard place-value (base) arithmetic.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 707, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00708', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Which character encoding standard supports the largest number of including characters from various languages and symbols?', '["BCD (Binary Coded Decimal)", "EBCDIC (Extended Binary Coded Decimal Interchange Code)", "ASCII (American Standard Code for Information Interchange)", "Unicode", "UTF-8 (Unicode Transformation Format bit)"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Option 1: Primarily used for representing decimal digits (0-9) in binary very limited in scope. Option 2: An older character encoding used mainly in IBM mainframes. Supports fewer characters compared to Unicode', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 708, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00709', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'BCD equivalent of 7310. 7310 BCD w.h', '["1110011 BCD", "01110011 BCD", "11101010 BCD", "11100001 BCD", "011100112"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "01110011 BCD". This follows from converting/calculating the given number(s) using standard place-value (base) arithmetic.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 709, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00710', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What is the result of the addition 5 + (-3) using 8-bit 2''s complement representation?', '["000000102", "000000112", "111111012", "000010002", "111111002"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Choose the second number and turn it into one''s complement. It can be done by inverting the number. .Kfka fojk ,nd 3 = 000000112 One''s complement of 3 add 1 and turn it into two''s complement', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 710, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00711', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What is the final result in decimal form of the following calculation?', '["125", "133", "152", "167", "172"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Step Convert all the numbers into decimal. The reason for this is it''s easier to perform operations like addition and multiplication when all numbers are in the same base. since the answers are provided in this approach ensures accuracy and consistency', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 711, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00712', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Convert the decimal number 156.75 to binary. 156.75', '["10011100.112", "10011101.012", "10011100.1012", "10011101.102", "10011100.1112"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "10011100.112". This follows from converting/calculating the given number(s) using standard place-value (base) arithmetic.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 712, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00713', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'In the context of encoding systems like ASCII and what does backward compatibility refer to?', '["The ability of older encoding standards to understand text encoded using newer standards. kj", "The ability of newer encoding standards to understand text encoded using older standards", "The ability of encoding systems to handle text written in reverse order", "The ability of encoding systems to compress text data for backward storage", "The ability of encoding systems to encrypt text data for backward transmission"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Backward compatibility in the context of encoding systems like ASCII and Unicode refers to the ability of newer encoding standards to understand and interpret text that has been encoded using older standards', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 713, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00714', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'In the binary all numbers and special characters are formed by which unique combination?', '["Eight Bits", "Eight bytes", "Twelve Bits", "Eight character", "Four bytes"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Option 1: Correct. In binary each character and special symbols) is encoded using a unique combination of 8 bits (1 byte). This is the standard in systems like ASCII and extended character encoding. Option 2: Incorrect', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 714, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00715', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'A = 0.7510 + 100110102 B = 2''s complement of 45 - 2''s complement of 31 What are the values of A and B respectively?', '["10010001.11, 00011101", "00001111.01, 10101101", "1001110.11, 00000111", "01100010 .11, 11110001", "10011010.11, 00001110"]'::jsonb, 5, 'let''s solve for A 0.112 + 100110102 = 10011010.112 Then solve for B 4510 - 3110 = 1410 = 000011102 So A = 10011010.112 B = 000011102', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 715, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00716', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What is the decimal value that is equivalent to binary 1101011.10112?', '["107.687", "1723", "107.6875", "53.625", "21.625"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Let''s convert this binary number into decimal', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 716, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00717', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'An encryption system converts characters into binary values and XORs them with a key. The letter ''A'' represents the decimal 65. If the character is XORed with the key 011100012, what is the resulting binary value?', '["010001002", "101101012", "011101112", "101111112", "001101012"]'::jsonb, 5, 'let''s get the corresponding decimal value for D here. A → 65 B → 66 C → 67 D → 68 Information and Communication Technology 2026/04/02 1) L1 Now let''s get its binary value. oeka tys Now let''s XOR this with the given value. oeka 0 1 0 1 0 02 0 1 0 12 0 1 0 1 0 12', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 717, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00718', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'A certain text file takes 7016 bits to represent using a coding system called x. It takes 22410 bits to represent the same file in UTF -16 Unicode. What coding system is x?', '["BCD", "ASCII", "EBCDIC", "Gray code", "Data is"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Answer : 3) let''s convert the value 7016 to a decimal. Now let''s find the number of characters in that file. oeka tu number of characters Now let''s find the number of bits required to represent a character using the x coding system', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 718, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00719', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What is the answer when the one''s complement of 24 is subtracted from the two''s complement of -96?', '["100010002", "101000002", "100111112", "000110002", "100110002"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The one''s complement of any positive number is the binary representation of that number. the one''s complement of 24 is as follows. Now let''s find the two''s complement of -96 as follows', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 719, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00720', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Which of the following devices most commonly uses BCD for displaying outputs?', '["High-performance gaming processors", "Digital voltmeters and clocks", "Machine learning processors", "GPS systems", "Storage devices like"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: Incorrect. High-performance gaming processors don''t use BCD (Binary-Coded Decimal) for output. They process data in binary for speed and performance. Tjqka Option 2: Correct. These devices commonly use BCD to display numeric values like voltages and time', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 720, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00721', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What is the range of numbers that can be represented in 2''s complement with 8 bits?', '["0 to 255", "-128 to 127", "-127 to 127", "-256 to 255", "1 to 128"]'::jsonb, 2, '2''s complement notation It is used to represent signed integers (both positive and negative)', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 721, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00722', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What is the decimal equivalent of the hexadecimal number BC1216?', '["47146", "46126", "48146", "49116", "45036"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Let''s convert the hexadecimal number BC1216 into decimal. BC1216', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 722, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00723', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What is the main limitation of the BCD character representation method?', '["Limited to representing numeric characters only", "Complex implementation", "Lack of compatibility with modern systems", "High memory usage", "Poor performance for non-Latin languages"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Option 1: Correct. BCD (Binary -Coded Decimal) is a character representation method primarily used for representing decimal numbers in binary form. Each digit of a decimal number is encoded in 4 bits', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 723, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00724', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What is the one''s complement of decimal -12 ?', '["000011002", "111100112", "001100112", "111101002", "111100002"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Step 1 : Convert -12 to binary. In binary form -12 is represented as 000011002. Step 1: -12 Step 2: Apply 1''s complement to the binary representation. Complement means flipping all the bits (changing 0 to 1 and 1 to 0). the complement of 000011002 is 111100112. Step 2: 111100112', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 724, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00725', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'How much memory capacity does the EBCDIC coding system use to represent one character?', '["4 bit", "8 bit", "16 bit", "48 bit", "7 bit"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The EBCDIC coding system uses 8 bits to represent one character. EBCDIC The ASCII coding system uses 7 bits to represent one character. ASCII The BCD coding system uses 4 bits to represent one character. BCD Unicode uses 16 bits to represent one character. 3', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 725, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00726', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Given the 8-bit 2''s complement binary number 1110 1101, what is its decimal equivalent?', '["-19", "-35", "-29", "-27", "2-"]'::jsonb, 1, 'To find the decimal equivalent of the 8-bit 2''s complement binary number 11101101, follow these 8-bit 2 1 Identify if it''s a negative number The leftmost bit (1) indicates that it''s a negative number since it''s 1 in 2''s complement', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 726, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00727', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What is the BCD value of 202610 ?', '["010 0000 010 0110BCD", "1001 0110 1001 0110BCD", "0010 0000 0010 0110BCD", "1001 110 1001 110 1001BCD", "0010 0000 0010 01102"]'::jsonb, 3, 'To find the Binary-Coded Decimal (BCD) value of 202610, we need to convert each digit of the decimal number into its 4-bit binary representation. 202610 Binary-coded Decimal (BCD) w.h fidhd', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 727, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00728', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'In a computer the 8 -bit binary number 11010110 is stored. If this number represents a signed integer using two''s what is the decimal value?', '["42", "-38", "-42", "-45", "38"]'::jsonb, 3, 'First subtract 1 to convert two''s complement to one''s complement. 1 0 1 0 1 02 -12 1 0 1 0 1 0 12 Now the bits of this one''s complement number need to be inverted. oeka 110101012 → 001010102 Now let''s convert this number to decimal', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 728, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00729', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What is the minimum number of bits needed to represent the hexadecimal number A7C416?', '["4 bits", "12 bits", "16 bits", "8 bits", "2 bits"]'::jsonb, 3, 'A hexadecimal number is base 16, meaning each digit in a hexadecimal number can be represented by 4 bits. to determine the minimum number of bits needed to represent a hexadecimal you can multiply the number of hexadecimal digits by 4', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 729, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00730', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'D̅(BC + BD̅̅̅̅̅) + CC̅̅̅̅. Solve this Boolean expression', '["CD\u0305", "B + C", "BCD\u0305", "C\u0305 + D\u0305", "B\u0305 + D\u0305"]'::jsonb, 4, 'We simplify this expression using Boolean laws', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 730, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00731', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What is the decimal equivalent of hexadecimal number B1A?', '["2891", "2980", "2981", "2826", "2842"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Let''s convert Hexadecimal B1A into decimal B1A', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 731, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00732', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What is the result of taking the one''s complement of the binary number 1011012?', '["0100102", "01001012", "01011002", "01011102", "10110102"]'::jsonb, 1, 'One''s complement is a way to represent negative numbers in binary by flipping all the bits of a positive number to get its negative counterpart. For flipping 0s to 1s and 1s to 0s in a binary number represents its one''s complement. 1ys 0, 1 0 1 0 12 → 0 1 0 1 02', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 732, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00733', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Which encoding system does support that improves character representation?', '["ASCII", "Unicode", "ISO-8859-1", "ANSI", "EBCDIC"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is Unicode because supports this encoding system to enhance character representation', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 733, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00734', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'A certain digital clock shows time in binary-coded decimal (BCD) format. If the current time is will be the binary representation in BCD?', '["0001 0101 : 0100 0111", "0011 0001 : 0010 1101", "0010 0101 : 0101 0001", "0001 0100 : 0101 0100", "0110 0111 : 0111 0100"]'::jsonb, 1, 'To represent the time in Binary-Coded Decimal (BCD), each digit is converted into its 4-bit binary equivalent. Binary-coded Decimal (BCD) u', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 734, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00735', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Which of the following answer is equivalent to value which can be obtained after converting BCD to octal value 2458?', '["000101100100BCD", "0001011001012", "000101100101BCD", "0001011001002", "101100101BCD"]'::jsonb, 3, 'let''s convert 2458 to decimal number. 2458 2 4 5 82 × 2 81 × 4 80 × 5 128 32 5 128 + 32 + 5 = 165 16510 let''s convert 16510 to BCD code. 16510 BCD 16510 1 6 5 0001 0110 0101 0001 0110 0101BCD', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 735, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00736', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Select the answer that shows the number 76 in BCD and binary respectively. 76 hk BCD', '["0111110BCD , 011101002", "01001100BCD , 011101102", "01010101BCD , 010011002", "01110110BCD , 010011002", "01110110BCD , 010101002"]'::jsonb, 4, 'First let''s convert this number to BCD. Now let''s convert this number to binary. oeka', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 736, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00737', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'If the ASCII value of is 66, How can we represent the word ''DEOGEN''?', '["01000100 01001111 01000111 01000101 01001110", "01000100 01000101 01001111 01000111 01000101 01001110", "01000100 01000101 01001100 01000111 01000101 01001110", "01000100 01000000 01001111 01000100 01000101 01001110", "01000111 01000101 01001111 01000100 01000101 01001111"]'::jsonb, 2, 'We need to find the binary ASCII representation of the word ''DEOGEN''. Let''s break it "DEOGEN" hk jpkfha D → ASCII value is (ASCII w.h) 68 → Binary E → ASCII value is (ASCII w.h) 69 → Binary O → ASCII value is (ASCII w.h) 79 → Binary G → ASCII value is (ASCII w', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 737, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00738', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', '8 bit 2''s complement of a decimal number called X is 110100012. What is the value of that X?', '["46", "-46", "47", "-47", "208"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Given the 2''s complement of a one bit must be subtracted from the second complement to find its first complement. fojk wvq 1 0 1 0 12 - 12 1 0 1 0 02 When finding the negative number corresponding to the first those bits must be inversed', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 738, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00739', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Select the correct ASCII code for the word from the following answers', '["01000011 01100001 01101100 01100011 01110101 01101100 01100001 01100011 01100101", "01000011 01100001 01101100 01100011 01110101", "01000011 01100001 01101100 01100011 01110101 10100100 01001111 00110010 01100011", "01100100 01101000 01101100 01100101 01110010 01101100 01100001 01101111 01100011", "01000011 01100001 01101100 01100011 01110101 01101100 01100001 01110100 01100101"]'::jsonb, 5, 'To determine the correct ASCII code for the word ''Calculate'', we need to find the decimal ASCII code and then convert each character in the word to its ASCII binary representation. hk has a decimal ASCII value of 65. A ASCII w.h 65 has a decimal ASCII value of 97', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 739, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00740', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What is the binary equivalent to 0.62510 in decimal notation?', '["0.1112", "0.1012", "1.0102", "0.1002", "0.0012"]'::jsonb, 2, '0.625 × 2 = 1.250 ------- 1 0.250 × 2 = 0.500 ------- 0.500 × 2 = 1.000-------- 1 0.62510 = 0.1012 4', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 740, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00741', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'The Decimal value of the ASCII code of is 67. which ASCII values represent the characters and ?', '["1001111, 1010001", "1000011, 1000011", "1000010, 1000101", "1110011, 1100001", "1000011, 1000001"]'::jsonb, 3, 'In the ASCII encoding each character is assigned a unique numerical value. The ASCII value for is 67 in decimal. Since comes before in the its ASCII value is one which is 66', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 741, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00742', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What is the primary function of a full adder in digital circuits?', '["To perform addition of two binary numbers with a carry-in input. carry-in wdodkhla", "To perform subtraction of two binary numbers", "To multiply two binary numbers", "To divide two binary numbers", "To compare two binary numbers"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The basic function of a full adder in digital circuits is to add two binary numbers with a carry-in input. In a full adder only addition takes place. All remaining calculations are done through addition. 2''s complements are also used for that. 5', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 742, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00743', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Which of the following represents the bitwise XNOR operation output value between the 2 binary numbers 110001112 and 100100102 ?', '["A916", "101010108", "170", "25216", "252"]'::jsonb, 3, 'XNOR operation between the given numbers 110001112 100100102 101010102 Information and Communication Technology 2026/05/02', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 743, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00744', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What is the correct 2''s complement binary representation of decimal -42?', '["10101012", "10101112", "110101102", "110101012", "001010112"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Calculating the 2''s complement of decimal -42. -42 2 .Kkh To find the 2''s complement binary representation of a negative decimal the following steps can be 2 yel( Convert the absolute value of the decimal number to binary', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 744, '2027 Quiz Series'),
