('alict_00759', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Which of the following statements about hexadecimal representation is TRUE?', '["Hexadecimal uses a base-2 system", "Hexadecimal digits range from 0-9", "Each hexadecimal digit can be represented by four binary bits. ixLHdxlhlau", "Hexadecimal is primarily used for everyday arithmetic. m%Odk wxl", "Hexadecimal is less compact than binary for representing large numbers"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Hexadecimal is a base-16 number system. Each hex digit (0-9 and A-F) corresponds exactly to 4 binary bits (a nibble). This makes it a compact and convenient way to represent binary data. Option 1: Hexadecimal uses base-16, not base-2 (which is binary)', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 759, '2027 Quiz Series'),
