('alict_00765', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What is the most suitable answer for getting the one''s complement of a binary number?', '["By flipping all the bits", "By adding 1 to the binary number", "By subtracting 1 from the binary number", "By flipping all the bits only if number is negative", "By performing a bitwise AND operation with all 1s 1 iu"]'::jsonb, 4, 'The one''s complement of a binary number is a method of representing negative numbers in binary form. In one''s complement positive numbers are represented exactly the same way as they are in standard binary notation. The bits remain unchanged for positive numbers', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 765, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00766', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Why are flip-flops essential in digital logic circuits?', '["To increase the speed of arithmetic operations in the processor. ilikfha wxl", "To convert analog signals into digital signals for processing", "To perform logical operations such as and NOT. NOT jeks", "To store and manage binary data and maintain state information within the circuit", "To generate high-frequency clock signals for the ix{d and Communication ;dlaIKh 2026"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Flip-flops are essential in digital logic circuits because they are used to store and manage binary data and maintain state information within the circuit', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 766, '2027 Quiz Series'),
