('alict_00769', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What is the main reason for using signed magnitude representation for integers?', '["It simplifies arithmetic operations", "It provides a unique representation for zero", "It is easy for humans to understand and interpret", "It requires less storage space than 2''s complement. thg 2 wvq bvla", "It eliminates the need for carry bits in addition. th"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Signed magnitude representation stores the sign (positive or negative) in the most significant bit and the magnitude in the remaining bits. This method is intuitive for as it clearly separates the sign and making it easier to read and understand', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 2027, 769, '2027 Quiz Series'),
