('alict_00845', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'In a multi-tasking operating which process state transition is managed by the short-term scheduler?', '["Blocked \u2192 Running", "Ready \u2192 Running", "Suspended \u2192 Terminated", "Running \u2192 Blocked", "New \u2192 Ready Odjk \u2192"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The short-term scheduler in a multi-tasking operating system is responsible for managing the transition from the Ready state to the Running state. Processes that are in the Ready state have all the necessary resources and are waiting for CPU time to execute', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', 2027, 845, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00846', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'Which of the following is a major use of CMOS in a personal computer?', '["Getting instructions for operations", "Keeping the settings of the basic input-output system for the power process", "Providing space for loading the operating system", "Keeping information for the output", "Holding inputs for processing. ioyd"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: CMOS is not involved in obtaining instructions for operations. This task is typically handled by the CPU (Central Processing Unit) through fetching instructions from the system''s such as RAM (Random Access Memory)', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', 2027, 846, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00847', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'Which of the following statements about the File Allocation Table (FAT) is correct?', '["FAT stores the actual data of files directly on the disk. FAT", "FAT is used to keep track of which disk blocks are allocated to which files. FAT", "FAT eliminates the need for a directory structure. FAT", "FAT allows random access to files without following linked clusters. FAT", "FAT is only used in Linux-based file systems. FAT"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: FAT does not store actual FAT Option 2: FAT maintains a table mapping each file to its disk showing which blocks are used and in what order. FAT Option 3: A directory structure is still needed to map file names to starting blocks. f', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', 2027, 847, '2027 Quiz Series'),
('alict_00848', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'What is a Program in execution called?', '["Function", "Process", "Instruction Wmfoia", "Procedure", "Paging"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: A block of code designed to perform a specific task. It is typically a reusable segment of a program but is not a program in execution. Option 2: A program in execution. It is an active entity with a program and other resources', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', 2027, 848, '2027 Quiz Series'),
