('alict_00894', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following statement(s) about the types of ROM is', '["Input", "Processing", "Output", "Storage", "None of the above"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "Input". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 894, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00895', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'How is data stored in ROM?', '["Temporarily using electrical charges", "Permanently using non-volatile methods", "Dynamically using transistors", "Temporarily using magnetic fields", "Permanently using volatile methods"]'::jsonb, 2, 'ROM (Read-Only Memory) stores data permanently using non-volatile methods. ROM u.ska Data in ROM is written during the manufacturing process or through specific programming (like in EEPROM)', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 895, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00896', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'What is the main advantage of EEPROM over EPROM?', '["It can be erased using ultraviolet light", "It allows for data erasure and reprogramming through electrical signals. th", "It has a much higher storage capacity", "It is faster than RAM", "It can only be written once"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: This is a characteristic of not EEPROM. EPROM requires UV light exposure to erase data. EPROM Option 2: Correct. This is the key advantage of EEPROM. Data can be erased and rewritten making it more convenient and easier to update than EPROM', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 896, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00897', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'A cache memory is located in which of the following?', '["Multi Media Projector", "Dot Matrix Printer", "CPU", "LCD Monitor", "Scanner"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "CPU". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 897, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00898', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which type of RAM is faster and used as cache memory?', '["DRAM", "SRAM", "SDRAM", "VRAM", "DDR4"]'::jsonb, 2, 'DRAM (Dynamic RAM) - Wrong Answer Used as main system memory (RAM). m%Odk Slower than SRAM because it requires constant refreshing to maintain data. SRAM Commonly found in computers and mobile devices as primary RAM. cx.u 2', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 898, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00899', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'A computer has three RAM drives. They run at a clock speed of and 4800MHz respectively. In which clock speed will the RAM system run at?', '["5600 MHz", "4800 MHz", "4600 MHz", "4200 MHz", "3200 MHz"]'::jsonb, 5, 'When you mix RAM your computer runs at the speed of the slowest RAM Tn RAM 1. Synchronization is key. All parts of your RAM system must work together at the same speed for data to transfer correctly. 2. Memory controllers are simple', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 899, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00900', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which component of the abstract model of information is analogous to the Central Processing Unit (CPU) in a computer (CPU) iudk : 2) Explanation', '["Input", "Processing", "Output", "Storage", "None of the above"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "Input". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 900, 'A/L Past Paper Series')
