('alict_00979', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following is not a step of parallel computing?', '["Dividing the computer program into segments", "Segments are again divided into smaller segments. LKav", "The workload is divided among the computers", "Result of these steps is one output", "Forwarding the divided segments into the processor. LKavkh fldgia ilikhg fhduq"]'::jsonb, 3, 'A running program is divided in to small sections and sent into the processor one after the other is known as parallel computing while a set of computers working together to perform a specific task is known as Grid Computing. Steps of Parallel computing. 1', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 979, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00980', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following advancements primarily contributed to the development of computers that could perform multiple tasks simultaneously?', '["Magnetic Tape", "Multicore Processors. ilik", "Floppy Disks", "Vacuum Tubes", "Assembly Language"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "Multicore Processors. ilik". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 980, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_00981', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'This volatile device is a part of the CPU that acts as a buffer between the physical memory and the processor when running applications of the computer and it improves performance. What is this device?', '["RAM (Random Access Memory) RAM is a type of volatile memory used to temporarily store data and machine code currently being used by the computer. It allows for fast read and write access to a storage medium that is essential for the system''s performance. While RAM significantly impr oves the performance of a computer by providing quick access to data for the it is not located within the CPU itself. RAM is part of the system memory and serves as a broader workspace for the entire operating system and not specifically as a buffer between the CPU and the physical memory. RAM hkq oekg th bv CPU blauka ,nd th CPU RAM hkq fldgila CPU n*rhla jev bvla fiajh lrhs'' 2025", "RAM", "ROM", "L1 cache", "Registers"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Correct answer: "L1 cache". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 981, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
