('alict_01013', 4, 'Computer Systems & Architecture', 'Which of the following best describes the printing mechanism of a dot matrix printer?', '["Printing is achieved using a laser beam to create static charges on a drum. fnrhla", "A printhead with pins strikes an inked ribbon to create characters on paper. lvodis", "Printing is achieved using heat to transfer ink from a ribbon to paper", "An electrostatic charge attracts toner to a drum and transfers it to paper", "Ink is sprayed directly onto paper from a nozzle in precise patterns"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "A printhead with pins strikes an inked ribbon to create characters on paper. lvodis". This reflects how this hardware component/device is defined and used in a standard computer system.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Computer Systems & Architecture', NULL, 1013, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
