('alict_01066', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'Which of the following is an example of a network topology?', '["Star", "Circle", "Sphere", "Node", "Hub"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "Star". This follows from standard networking concepts (protocols, topologies, or the OSI/TCP-IP model).', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1066, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01067', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'What is the primary purpose of edge computing in applications?', '["To centralize data processing in cloud", "To reduce latency by processing data closer to the", "To enhance security through", "To increase bandwidth for data", "To manage user interfaces more"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Real-time processing Many applications demand immediate responses to events or data changes. By processing data at the closer to the delay between data generation and processing is significantly reduced. This enables faster decision-making and more efficient operations', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1067, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01068', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'Which of the following is the protocol that is used to prevent data collision in the Ring topology?', '["CSMA", "Token Ring", "ALOHA", "Slotted ALOHA", "Telnet"]'::jsonb, 2, 'CSMA This protocol is used in Ethernet where devices can sense the carrier signal and detect collisions. It does not apply to ring topologies', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1068, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01069', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'What does the tracert command do in a networking context?', '["It tests the reachability of a host", "It displays the path taken by packets to a destination. th", "It configures network interfaces", "It measures the bandwidth of a connection", "It retrieves the IP address of a domain name"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The tracert command (short for "trace route") is used to trace the route that packets take from the source to a destination host in a network. It provides information about each node along the including the time it takes for packets to travel to each helping diagnose network issues', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1069, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01070', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'Which of the following IP addresses is not a Class D IP address?', '["224.0.10.1", "243.0.10.1", "230.20.10.67", "233.233.233.233", "225.0.54.5"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Class D IP addresses are used for multicast groups and range from 224.0.0.0 to 239.255.255.255. Let''s analyze each of the given IP addresses to determine which one is not a Class D olajd mrdihl Let''s go through the given options 1) 224.0.10', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1070, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01071', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'Which of the following is not a commonly used network topology?', '["Star topology", "Mesh topology", "Ring topology", "Line topology", "Tree topology"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Star Topology Star topology is a widely used network topology where each node (computer or device) is connected to a central hub or switch. The hub acts as a central point of managing data traffic between the nodes', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1071, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01072', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'A = Session Layer - ieis = Transport Layer - = Presentation Layer - = Data Link Layer - = Application Layer - = Physical Layer - = Network Layer - is the correct order of the above layers for the OSI data transmission model?', '["ECBDAGF", "DGECABF", "FDCGABE", "ECABGDF", "CFABEDG"]'::jsonb, 4, 'The OSI (Open Systems Interconnection) model is a conceptual framework used to understand and describe how different networking protocols and technologies interact to facilitate communication between devices in a network', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1072, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01073', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'What is the network address for the IP 192.168.5.130 with a subnet mask of', '["192.168.5.0", "192.168.5.128", "192.168.5.64", "192.168.5.192", "255.255.255.128 Answer"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Step 1: A /25 subnet mask means 25 bits are used for the network and the remaining 7 bits are for hosts (32 - 25 = 7). /25 - 25 = 7). This gives 2⁷ = 128 total IP addresses per subnet. Step 2: We calculate the subnet First subnet 192.168.5', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1073, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01074', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'Which device operates at the Data Link layer of the OSI model?', '["Router", "Hub", "Switch", "Repeater", "Firewall"]'::jsonb, 3, 'A router operates at the Network layer (Layer 3) of the OSI model. It routes data between different networks and determines the best path for data to travel. rjqgrhla OSI 2) A hub operates at the Physical layer (Layer 1) of the OSI model', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1074, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01075', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'Which of the following statements is true about the OSI (Open Systems Interconnection) model?', '["The Network layer is responsible for and terminating connections between applications", "The Data Link layer is responsible for end-to-end communication and error correction across the entire network", "The Transport layer provides reliable data transfer services to the upper layers and is responsible for flow and error recovery", "The Presentation layer handles the routing of data packets between different networks and subnets", "The Session layer is responsible for packet forwarding including routing through intermediate routers"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "The Transport layer provides reliable data transfer services to the upper layers and is responsible for flow and error recovery". This follows from standard networking concepts (protocols, topologies, or the OSI/TCP-IP model).', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1075, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01076', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'A university wants to separate its Wi-Fi network for students and while still connecting both to the internet. Which device is MOST responsible for managing this traffic separation?', '["Repeater", "Hub", "Router", "Switch", "Modem"]'::jsonb, 3, 'A router is responsible for separating and managing traffic between different networks student Wi-Fi and staff Wi-Fi) while still providing access to the internet. rjqgrhla A switch only separates devices within the same network (LAN), not different networks', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1076, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01077', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'Which of the following statements about data transmission methods is most accurate and multicasting?', '["Unicasting sends data to a single destination while broadcasting sends data to all devices on the and multicasting sends data to a specific group of devices. Unicasting", "Broadcasting is the most efficient method for sending data to a large number of devices on a network", "Multicasting requires special network protocols but offers better efficiency than unicasting for sending data to a group of devices. nyq", "All network devices can send and receive data using broadcasting and multicasting methods", "Unicasting is the only method that guarantees reliable delivery of data to the destination device. Unicasting"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "Unicasting sends data to a single destination while broadcasting sends data to all devices on the and multicasting sends data to a specific group of devices. Unicasting". This follows from standard networking concepts (protocols, topologies, or the OSI/TCP-IP model).', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1077, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01078', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'In which of the following describes a secure method for verifying customer identity during transactions?', '["Username and Password", "IP Address Tracking", "One Time Password", "Cookies", "Simple Click Agreement"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: While commonly this method alone is not considered highly secure because passwords can be stolen or guessed. wkqudk yels Option 2: This is not a reliable method for verifying as IP addresses can change or be spoofed', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1078, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01079', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'What does the term "bandwidth" refer to in networking?', '["The physical distance between devices in a network", "The amount of data that can be transmitted in a fixed amount of time", "The number of devices connected to a network", "The type of cables used in a network", "The security level of a network"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The term bandwidth in networking refers to the amount of data that can be transmitted over a network in a fixed amount of time. It is usually measured in bits per second (bps), kilobits per second megabits per second or gigabits per second', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1079, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01080', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'Which of the following commands is issued to identify that which computer or router not functioning as expected in a computer network?', '["Netstat", "Ping", "IPConfig", "Tracert", "Hostname"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Correct answer: "Tracert". This follows from standard networking concepts (protocols, topologies, or the OSI/TCP-IP model).', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1080, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01081', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'Consider the IP address 10.1.2.5 and the subnet mask 255.255.255.192. How many hosts can be directly connected to this network?', '["30", "62", "126", "254", "51"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "62". This follows from standard networking concepts (protocols, topologies, or the OSI/TCP-IP model).', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1081, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01082', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'You are given an IP address of 192.168.1.0 with a subnet mask of 255.255.255.224. How many subnets and hosts per subnet are possible?', '["8 30 hosts per subnet", "6 32 hosts per subnet", "16 14 hosts per subnet", "4 64 hosts per subnet", "2 128 hosts per subnet"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "8 30 hosts per subnet". This follows from standard networking concepts (protocols, topologies, or the OSI/TCP-IP model).', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1082, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01083', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'You are sending a picture from your phone to a friend using a messaging app. The picture is 640 kilobytes (KB) in and your mobile network allows you to upload at a speed of 512 kilobits per second Tnf.a 640 kilobytes (KB) cx.u 512 kilobits per second bv 1 byte = 8 how long will it take to send the 640 KB picture with an upload speed of 512', '["5 seconds", "8 seconds", "10 seconds", "12 seconds", "15 seconds"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "10 seconds". This follows from standard networking concepts (protocols, topologies, or the OSI/TCP-IP model).', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1083, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01084', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'Which server type is typically responsible for hosting virtual providing virtualized and managing them efficiently across a network?', '["DNS Server", "Server", "Virtualization Server", "FTP Server", "Proxy Server"]'::jsonb, 3, 'DNS Server A DNS server translates domain names into IP allowing users to access websites using human-readable names instead of numerical IP addresses. It is not responsible for hosting or managing virtual machines', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1084, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01085', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'What is the most efficient network topology that uses more wires to connect each computer to every other computer in a computer u iu.u', '["Bus tropology", "Hybrid tropology", "Ring tropology", "Mash tropology", "Star tropology"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Bus topology In a bus all computers are connected to a single central known as the bus or backbone. It uses the least amount of but if the central cable the entire network goes down. It is simple but not very reliable or scalable', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1085, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01086', 9, 'Data Communication & Networking', 'In which application is analog signal transmission commonly used?', '["Internet communication", "Audio transmission over radio waves", "Sending data between computers", "Digital television broadcasting", "Wireless network communication"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "Audio transmission over radio waves". This follows from standard networking concepts (protocols, topologies, or the OSI/TCP-IP model).', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Data Communication & Networking', NULL, 1086, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01087', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which of the following scenarios demonstrates real-time data processing?', '["Processing monthly electricity bills", "A medical system monitoring patient heart rates. frda.Skaf.a iamkaok", "Preparing a quarterly income report for a business", "Sorting customer feedback into a database", "Preparing a weekly stock inventory report"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "A medical system monitoring patient heart rates. frda.Skaf.a iamkaok". This follows from standard relational database concepts/SQL rules applied to the scenario described.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1087, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01088', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which of the following are the main types of services provided by cloud computing?', '["Hardware as a Service Platform as a Service Storage as a Service", "Infrastructure as a Service Platform as a Service Software as a Service", "Networking as a Service Platform as a Service Database as a Service", "Infrastructure as a Service Database as a Service Software as a Service", "Computing as a Service Platform as a Service Storage as a Service"]'::jsonb, 2, 'These are the three main types of services provided by cloud computing. 1. Infrastructure as a Service Provides virtualized computing resources over the such as and networking', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1088, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01089', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Based on the information provided in the table the correct answers for C and G C G 4) Explanation', '["18210, 1716", "18210, 7710", "18216, 7710", "18210, 7716", "18810, 7716 So the correct answer is answer number"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "18210, 1716". This follows from standard relational database concepts/SQL rules applied to the scenario described.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1089, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01090', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Based on the information provided in the table the correct answers for E and D', '["1011 01102, 0111 01012", "1011 01102, 0111 01112", "1011 11102, 0111 01012", "1001 01102, 0111 01012", "1011 01102, 0111 00012"]'::jsonb, 2, 'According to the table the answers can be obtained. So the correct answer is answer number 2). 4', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1090, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01091', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'What is an entity in the context of a database?', '["A single column in a table", "A specific SQL query", "A distinct object or thing in the database", "A type of data encryption", "A database index"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "A distinct object or thing in the database". This follows from standard relational database concepts/SQL rules applied to the scenario described.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1091, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01092', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which of the following statements correctly distinguishes between an entity and an attribute in a database context?', '["An entity represents a real-world while an attribute is a property that describes the entity", "An entity is always but attributes can be of any data type", "Entities only exist in relational whereas attributes exist in all types of databases", "Attributes are more important than entities because they store the actual data", "Entities describe characteristics of attributes"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "An entity represents a real-world while an attribute is a property that describes the entity". This follows from standard relational database concepts/SQL rules applied to the scenario described.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1092, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01093', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'In a relation between the entities the type and condition of the relation should be specified. That is called as______attribute', '["Simple attribute", "Composite attribute", "Multivalued attribute", "Key attribute", "Descriptive attribute"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Correct answer: "Descriptive attribute". This follows from standard relational database concepts/SQL rules applied to the scenario described.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1093, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01094', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'What does it mean when an attribute is described as "multivalued"?', '["It can take on only one value at any time. th", "It can take on multiple values for each instance of an entity. th", "It is dependent on another attribute for its value. th tys w.h", "It is always null or empty. th", "It must be unique across all instances. th"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: This describes a single-valued not a multivalued attribute. A single-valued attribute can have only one value per entity instance nyq Option 2: This is the correct definition of a multivalued attribute', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1094, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01095', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'What type of database system is most suitable for computer-aided design?', '["Relational model", "Flat file model", "Network model", "Object relational model", "Hierarchical model"]'::jsonb, 4, 'A computer-aided design (CAD) system typically involves managing and manipulating complex data such as geometric hierarchies of and relationships among objects. The object relational model is the most suitable for such systems due to the following reasons', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1095, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01096', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'What is the purpose of a composite primary key?', '["To establish a many-to-many relationship between tables. j.=", "To uniquely identify a record using multiple columns", "To enforce data integrity across multiple tables. fndfyda j.=", "To improve query performance by creating a composite index", "To reduce data redundancy by combining related columns"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is 2) To uniquely identify a record using multiple columns. A composite primary key combines two or more columns in a table to form a unique identifier for each record. This is particularly useful when no single column alone can uniquely identify records', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1096, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01097', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'In the context of relational which of the following characteristics is unique to many -to-many relationships?', '["Requires each table to have a unique identifier. y\u00f7kd.ekSula", "Requires two foreign keys in one of the original tables", "Needs a separate table to establish the relationship", "Cannot exist without primary keys", "Allows records in both tables to remain independent. j.= foflysu"]'::jsonb, 3, 'In the context of relational many -to-many relationships require a separate known as a junction or bridge to establish the relationship between the two original tables', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1097, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01098', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Why would you avoid storing derived attributes directly in a table?', '["To improve query performance", "To avoid redundancy and inconsistency", "To save storage space in the database", "To allow derived attributes to be queried independently", "To enforce referential integrity. fhduq"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Storing derived attributes directly in a table is avoided primarily to prevent redundancy and which is why the correct answer is Option 2. Derived attributes are values that can be calculated or derived from other data in the database', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1098, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01099', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which of the following attributes is not represented in a database table?', '["Single valued attributes", "Multivalued attributes", "Stored attributes", "Key attributes", "Derived attributes"]'::jsonb, 5, 'In a database different types of attributes are represented to store and manage data efficiently. Single- valued attributes (option 1) store only one value per record and are directly present in like a person''s age or name', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1099, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01100', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'In the provided is a _________ attribute. What is the best match for the given blank?', '["Simple", "Descriptive", "Composite", "Derived", "Key"]'::jsonb, 2, 'In this the attribute is considered descriptive because it provides additional information about the interaction between the user and the movie', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1100, 'A/L Past Paper Series')
