('alict_01263', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'A <video> tag with autoplay works on desktop but not on mobile. What''s the hidden culprit? iajhxl%Sh jdokh <video> desktop tfla cx.u je', '["Missing muted attribute", "Browser doesn''t support MP4", "Video file is corrupted", "Add playsinline attribute", "Use poster attribute"]'::jsonb, 1, 'On mobile most browsers block autoplay for videos with sound to prevent unwanted data usage and to improve the user experience. To ensure autoplay works on mobile the video must be muted', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1263, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01264', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which of the following SQL statements will change all occurrences of to in the attribute of the CUSTOMER table?', '["UPDATE CUSTOMER SET City = WHERE City =", "MODIFY CUSTOMER SET City = WHERE City =", "UPDATE CUSTOMER SET City = INTO City =", "UPDATE CUSTOMER CHANGE City = TO", "UPDATE CUSTOMER SET City = WHERE City !="]'::jsonb, 1, 'This statement correctly uses the SQL UPDATE command to modify existing records in a table. The SET clause specifies the new value to be assigned to the City while the WHERE clause ensures that only records with City equal to are updated', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1264, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01265', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'After an attribute maps to a what is it called?', '["Table with a foreign key", "Separate table with a primary key", "Column", "Primary key column", "Foreign key column"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: This option is incorrect because a table with a foreign key describes a relationship between not what an attribute becomes. An attribute does not transform into an entire table', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1265, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01266', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'What does the <caption> tag do in a table?', '["It defines the style for the table", "It adds a border to the table", "It defines a row for the table", "It adds a header to the table", "It provides a title for the table"]'::jsonb, 5, '• Explanation of the <caption> Tag. The immediately after the opening for users and assistive technologies to understand what the table represents. For a table of sales data might use the myiq • Why Option 5 is Correct', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1266, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01267', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Consider the following relations from a database used to manage a library iuqodhlska Publisher_phone) Which of the following is NOT a foreign key in this schema?', '["Book_id in the LOAN relation", "Book_id in the BOOK relation", "Member_id in the LOAN relation", "Publisher_id in the BOOK relation", "Publisher_id in the PUBLISHER relation"]'::jsonb, 2, 'A foreign key is an attribute that references the primary key of another table. In the BOOK Book_id uniquely identifies each book and acts as the primary not a foreign key. Since it does not reference another it cannot be considered a foreign key', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1267, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01268', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which attribute in an element associates it with a specific CSS style sheet?', '["class", "id", "rel", "style", "href"]'::jsonb, 3, 'In the "rel" attribute is used to specify the relationship between the current document and the linked resource. When linking to a CSS setting "rel" to "stylesheet" associates the document with that CSS allowing it to style the content. oekg "rel"', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1268, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01269', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which attribute is stored as a separate table?', '["Entity", "Relationship", "Primary key", "Multivalued attribute", "Foreign key"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Option 1: This option is incorrect because an entity represents a real-world object (such as Student or Book) and is stored as a table not as an attribute stored separately. Option 2: This option is incorrect because relationships describe how entities are connected', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1269, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01270', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which attribute of the <audio> tag enables the display of playback controls such as pause and volume?', '["src", "autoplay", "controls", "loop", "preload"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Src Specifies the audio file source but does not enable playback controls. 2) Autoplay Automatically starts playing the audio when the page loads. 3) Controls The controls attribute in the pause and volume. <audio', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1270, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
