('alict_01272', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'What does the attribute signify in the context of a <link> tag?', '["It specifies the relationship between the current document and an external CSS file. th", "It links a file to the document. th f.dkqjla", "It defines inline styles within the", "It applies CSS styles only to", "It creates a new document for CSS definitions. th CSS"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Option 1: Correct. The attribute in a CSS stylesheet. This is the standard way to apply external CSS to an document. CSS Example Option 2: Incorrect. The Option 3: Incorrect', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1272, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01273', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'You create a link to download a PDF tlla nd.; ine¢hla', '["The server doesn''t set the Content-Disposition header. fiajdodhlh Content-Disposition", "Missing", "The download attribute only works with images", "Use instead", "The browser blocks downloads from untrusted sites"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The issue lies with the server configuration. When a link is the browser relies on the server''s instructions for how to handle the linked file', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1273, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01274', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which attribute is used to define Inline styles?', '["Class", "Style", "Id", "Font", "Group"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Class Used to specify a class for an which can be styled using but it is not used for inline styles. th 2) Style This attribute is used to apply CSS styles directly to an element', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1274, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01275', 7, 'Database Management Systems', 'Which of the following statements about 1NF is correct?', '["Tables can have repeating groups", "Each field must contain atomic values", "Primary key is optional", "Multi-valued attributes are allowed", "Data can be stored in unstructured format"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "Each field must contain atomic values". This follows from standard relational database concepts/SQL rules applied to the scenario described.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Database Management Systems', NULL, 1275, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
