('alict_01456', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'Which of the following statements accurately describes the significance of "universal gates" in digital logic?', '["They are the only gates capable of performing arithmetic operations. wxl", "They can be used to implement any Boolean function without requiring other types of gates", "They are designed to operate at any voltage making them universally compatible", "They are the fastest logic gates leading to minimal propagation delay. ,nd", "They are used to create the most power-efficient logic circuits"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The term "universal gate" refers to a logic gate that can be used to construct any other basic logic gate etc.) or any Boolean function. -universal gate- hk moh This means that with just one type of universal you can build any complex digital circuit', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1456, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01457', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'Consider a digital circuit where only NAND gates are available. Which of the following Boolean expressions can be directly implemented using a single NAND gate?', '["A.B", "A", "A+B", "A + B", "A \u2295 B"]'::jsonb, 2, 'A NOT operation can be achieved using a single-input NAND gate (connecting both inputs together). Option 1: The AND operation requires two NAND so it cannot be done in a single NAND gate', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1457, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01458', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'Given the Boolean expression (A + B̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅). (C̅ + D), and if inputs A = 0, B = 1 and 1, what are the possible outputs based on different values of D?', '["A only. A", "B only. B", "C only. C", "A and B only A B", "B and C only B C"]'::jsonb, 2, 'By building a truth table for all possible values of C and we can easily determine the outputs corresponding to different instances. C D A B C D (A + B̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅) (C̅ + D) (A + B̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅)', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1458, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01459', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'Given the Boolean expression A̅B + AC̅, how many minimum NAND gates are required to implement this circuit using only NAND gates?', '["3", "4", "5", "6", "8"]'::jsonb, 3, 'To determine how many NAND gates are required to implement the Boolean expression A̅B + AC̅ using only NAND we must first break down the logic operations in the expression. The expression involves three basic AND OR', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1459, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01460', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', '(A̅⨁B)AB̅̅̅̅ is equivalent iudk 3) Let''s simplify the above Boolean expression using Boolean lruq'' = (A̅⨁B)AB̅̅̅̅ = (A̿B + A̅B̅)AB̅̅̅̅ = (AB + A̅B̅)AB̅̅̅̅ Inverse law', '["A", "BD", "1", "AD", "AD+BC"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "A". This follows from evaluating the given Boolean expression / logic circuit using standard gate truth tables and Boolean algebra rules.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1460, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01461', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'Which of the following accurately describes the outputs of a full adder circuit?', '["It produces a single sum bit and no carry output. th", "It produces a sum bit and a carry-out bit", "It produces two sum bits and one carry-out bit. th sum folla carry-out tlla", "It produces a single carry-out bit and no sum output. Th", "It produces a sum bit and a carry-in bit"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Tuples are immutable which means they cannot be edited or manipulated so inserting items to a tuple using append will cause an error and the items in a tuple cannot be deleted so item deletion is also not supported by tuples. Tuple ksid Wm', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1461, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01462', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'Which of the following is a key characteristic of combinational circuits compared to sequential circuits?', '["They have memory elements", "Their output depends on current and past inputs", "They are typically slower in processing speed", "They do not contain any feedback paths", "They are primarily used for storing data"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Combinational circuits produce outputs based only on the current inputs and do not have memory or feedback paths. This is a key distinction from sequential which rely on current and past inputs due to the presence of memory elements and feedback', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1462, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01463', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'Which of the following statements about an SR Latch is TRUE?', '["It is a combinational circuit used primarily for arithmetic operations. th m%Odk wxl", "It has a clock input that controls when the state changes. tys", "When both S (Set) and R (Reset) inputs are 1, the output is always stable and predictable. S (Set) R (Reset) folu 1", "It is a fundamental building block of sequential capable of storing one bit of information. th", "Its output is solely dependent on its current not its previous state. tys"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Correct answer: "It is a fundamental building block of sequential capable of storing one bit of information. th". This follows from evaluating the given Boolean expression / logic circuit using standard gate truth tables and Boolean algebra rules.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1463, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01464', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'Which of the following statements is equivalent to the Boolean iudk o@ (BD + DD)1 + BC Answer : 4) Explanation', '["D", "BD", "BC", "1", "B"]'::jsonb, 3, 'x is defined as a dictionary containing two key-value "name": "John" and "age": 30. "age": 30 The print(x["age"]) statement accesses the value associated with the key "age" in the dictionary x. Since the value of "age" is 30, that value is printed to the output', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1464, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01465', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'A̅ + (D. D + 1. C). D̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅̅ Answer : 3) This Boolean expression can be simplified as follows', '["1", "0", "D\u0305", "D\u0305. C\u0305", "A. D. C\u0305 = 0A\u0305 + (DD + 1C)D\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305 = 0A\u0305 + (DD + 1C)\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305 + D\u0305 De Morgan''s Law"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "D̅". This follows from evaluating the given Boolean expression / logic circuit using standard gate truth tables and Boolean algebra rules.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1465, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
