('alict_01468', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'Which of the following Product of Sums (POS) expressions represents the K-map below?', '["(P + Q). (P + R\u0305). (Q + R + S). (Q + R\u0305 + S\u0305)", "(Q + R\u0305). (P + Q). (P + R\u0305 + S). (P + R + S\u0305)", "(P + Q). (P + R\u0305). (P\u0305 + Q + R + S). (P\u0305 + Q + R\u0305 + S\u0305)", "(P + Q). (P\u0305 + Q + R\u0305). (P + R\u0305 + S). (P + R + S\u0305)", "(P\u0305 + Q\u0305). (P\u0305 + R). (Q\u0305 + R\u0305 + S\u0305). (Q\u0305 + R + S)"]'::jsonb, 1, 'A Karnaugh map is a graphical method used to simplify Boolean expressions. For Product of Sums (POS) the 0''s in the K-map are grouped to derive a simplified expression as a product (AND) of maxterms (sum terms). ldfkda wdldrfhka" (Q + R + S) (Q + R̅ + S̅) (P + Q) (P + R̅)', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1468, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01469', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'A full adder takes three inputs', '["Sum = 0, Cout = 1", "Sum = 1, Cout = 1", "Sum = 0, Cout = 0", "Sum = 1, Cout = 0", "Invalid"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Step 1: Calculating the Sum To calculate the sum output of a full we use the XOR (exclusive OR) logic operation across all three and Cin. XOR returns 1 only when the number of 1s is odd', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1469, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
