('alict_01533', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'Consider the following SSOP Boolean expression (A. B. C + A. B̅. C + A. B. C̅), assume that you have 3 inputs as (A. B. C), (A. B̅. C), (A. B. C̅). Now if you want to turn these 3 inputs to a SPOS expression what gate should you use?', '["3 input AND gate", "3 input OR gate", "3 input NAND gate", "3 input NOR gate", "3 input XOR gate"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Answer 4, in the SSOP circuit we use an OR gate to get the sum at the end in order to make an SPOS using an SSOP expression we need to add a bar to the whole expression this can be achieved by replacing the final OR gate with a NOR gate. 5', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1533, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_01534', 3, 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', 'What is the correct SOP expression of the given POS expression?', '["(A. B) + (B. C) + (A\u0305. C)", "(A. B. C + A\u0305. B\u0305. C\u0305)", "(A\u0305. B. C\u0305 + A. B\u0305. C)", "(A\u0305. B\u0305. C + A. B\u0305. C\u0305 + A\u0305. B. C\u0305)", "(A + B\u0305) . (B + C\u0305) . (A\u0305 + C)"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "(A. B. C + A̅. B̅. C̅)". This follows from evaluating the given Boolean expression / logic circuit using standard gate truth tables and Boolean algebra rules.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Digital Electronics & Logic Circuits', NULL, 1534, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
