('alict_02045', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the following statements best describes the classification of systems?', '["Open systems are completely independent and do not interact with their while closed systems interact freely with external factors", "Natural systems are always while manmade systems are always open", "Living systems are typically exchanging energy and information with their while physical systems can be either open or closed", "Manmade systems are always physical systems and cannot be classified as living systems", "Closed systems are typically natural and do not allow the exchange of or information with their environment"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "Living systems are typically exchanging energy and information with their while physical systems can be either open or closed". This follows from the standard definitions of data, information, and ICT processing concepts.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', NULL, 2045, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02046', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the following best describes the primary purpose of an information system?', '["To manufacture physical products", "To store and retrieve information only", "To and distribute", "To manage human resources manually", "To design hardware components"]'::jsonb, 3, 'An information system is designed to support and decision-making by and distributing relevant information. It is a combination of and processes not limited to just storage or hardware design', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', NULL, 2046, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02047', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which invention during the Pre -Mechanical Era most fundamentally demonstrated the principle of symbolic data representation as a precursor to modern information systems?', '["The abacus used for arithmetic operations. wxl", "The development of papyrus scrolls in ancient Egypt", "The Antikythera mechanism for astronomical calculation", "Clay tablets from Mesopotamia used for trade records", "The quipu system used by the Incas to store numeric information"]'::jsonb, 5, 'This question targets knowledge of the conceptual roots of information processing. The focus is on how early tools moved from simple calculation or storage to symbolic abstraction and codified the basis of modern data systems. m%Yakh .Kkh olajd Option Incorrect', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', NULL, 2047, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
