('alict_02051', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'In which memory segment does the OS store temporary such as function parameters and return addresses?', '["Code Segment According to this it''s false. The code also known as the text stores the executable instructions of a not temporary data like function parameters and return addresses", "Data Segment According to this it''s false. The data segment stores global and static not temporary data related to function execution", "Stack Segment According to this it''s true. The stack segment is used to store temporary data such as function local and return addresses during function calls and execution", "Heap Segment According to this it''s false. The heap segment is used for dynamic memory where memory is allocated and freed during program not for temporary data like function parameters", "Instruction Segment According to this it''s false. The instruction segment is similar to the code storing the program''s executable not temporary data"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "Code Segment According to this it''s false. The code also known as the text stores the executable instructions of a not temporary data like function parameters and return addresses". This follows from the standard definitions of data, information, and ICT processing concepts.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', NULL, 2051, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02052', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'A small library used to keep track of borrowed books using a notebook. Now it uses a computer system to record which books are borrowed and f.k hk wdmiq ,nd fok igyka oeka th f.k hk wdmiq ,nd fok lrhs'' What is one advantage of using the computer-based system instead of the manual one?', '["The computer system guarantees zero errors in all borrowing transactions", "Human involvement in the library''s operations is no longer necessary", "It ensures books cannot be misplaced or lost", "It prevents all forms of data loss without any backups", "Records can now be and updated more efficiently"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Using a computer-based system improves data management. It saves time and reduces manual effort compared to flipping through pages in a notebook. mdol Option 1: Computers reduce errors but don''t guarantee zero errors ,mistakes can still happen', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', NULL, 2052, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02053', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'What type of system is used by top managers in a given organization?', '["Knowledge Management Systems", "Executive Support Systems", "Transaction Processing Systems. .kqfokq", "Management Information Systems", "Enterprise Resource Planning Systems"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "Executive Support Systems". This follows from the standard definitions of data, information, and ICT processing concepts.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', NULL, 2053, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02054', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the following correctly represents a common classification of information systems based on organizational function and decision-making level?', '["Transaction Processing System (TPS), Management Information System (MIS), Decision Support System (DSS), Executive Information System (EIS) .kqfokq", "Manual Semi-automated Fully Automated Intelligent System", "Primary Secondary Tertiary Support System", "Client Server Peer-to-Peer Distributed System fiajdfhdacl", "Structured Unstructured Dynamic Static System"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Option 1: Correct This is a widely accepted classification based on the levels of management and types of decision TPS (Transaction Processing System): Handles routine transactions (e.g., order entry)', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', NULL, 2054, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02055', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'In what is called a multi-dimensional array?', '["Arrays that use named keys instead of indices", "These are the arrays that have numeric indices", "These arrays can only store a fixed number of elements. wrd", "These arrays can store only elements of the same data type. wrd", "These are the arrays which are containing one or more arrays"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Option 1: This describes associative not multi-dimensional arrays. Associative arrays in PHP use string keys instead of numeric indices to store and access values. multi-dimensional arrays associative arrays', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', NULL, 2055, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02056', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'In the context of the Software Development Life Cycle which of the following activities is typically performed during the phase?', '["Writing code and implementing functionality", "Identifying and documenting system requirements", "Creating detailed architectural diagrams and data models", "Conducting unit and integration testing", "Deploying the system to the production environment"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: According to this it''s false to say this activity is typically performed during the phase', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', NULL, 2056, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02057', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'What is a key characteristic of machine-to-machine (M2M) coexistence?', '["Machines operate independently without", "Machines share information and work together without human", "Machines require constant human", "Machines are only used for physical", "Machines cannot adapt to changing"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The correct answer is 2) Machines share information and work together without human intervention. Explanation This is a key characteristic of machine-to-machine (M2M) where devices exchange data and perform tasks autonomously without needing human input', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', NULL, 2057, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02058', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'In the context of software what is the primary function of an ''interface agent''?', '["To improve system security by managing user access", "To facilitate communication between users and the software system", "To execute commands in the background without user input", "To optimize hardware performance", "To store user data securely"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: This is the role of security not interface agents. Option 2: Interface agents act as intermediaries that simplify or enhance user interaction with software often by providing or a user-friendly interface', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', NULL, 2058, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02059', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which modulation technique varies the amplitude of the carrier signal to transmit data?', '["FSK (Frequency Shift Keying)", "ASK (Amplitude Shift Keying)", "PSK (Phase Shift Keying)", "QAM (Quadrature Amplitude Modulation)", "PAM (Pulse Amplitude Modulation)"]'::jsonb, 2, 'FSK (Frequency Shift Keying) This technique varies the frequency of the carrier signal to represent different data bits. ASK (Amplitude Shift Keying) This technique varies the amplitude of the carrier signal to represent different data bits', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', NULL, 2059, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
