('alict_02070', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Which answer states the method(s) used to represent negative numbers in binary based number mdol Signed magnitude method', '["A only. A", "B only. B", "C only. C", "B and C Only B C", "All of the above"]'::jsonb, 5, '• Signed Magnitude Method The leftmost bit (Most Significant Bit - MSB) is used as a sign bit. 0 represents a positive and 1 represents a negative number. 0 Ok The remaining bits represent the magnitude (absolute value) of the number', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2070, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02071', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What is a key limitation of the Binary-Coded Decimal (BCD) system compared to the binary system?', '["BCD cannot represent fractional numbers", "Arithmetic operations in BCD are less efficient than in binary. BCD wxl", "BCD can only represent numbers up to 9", "BCD does not use the binary numeral system for representation", "BCD is not compatible with ASCII for encoding characters. BCD"]'::jsonb, 2, '• Option 1: Incorrect. BCD can represent fractional numbers using a fixed-point representation or BCD floating-point format. handling decimal points requires additional making it more complex than binary. BCD yg BCD Nd', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2071, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
