('alict_02073', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'The EBCDIC code system is used to represent one feature in memory format?', '["4 bit", "8 bit", "16 bit", "48 bit", "7 bit"]'::jsonb, 2, 'EBCDIC (Extended Binary Coded Decimal Interchange Code) is an 8 -bit character encoding system developed by IBM. It was primarily used in mainframes and early IBM computers. EBCDIC ,o gq 8 l Each character in EBCDIC is represented using 8 bits (1 byte)', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2073, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02074', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Which of the primarily used in digital circuits to minimize errors by ensuring that only one-bit changes at a time between successive values?', '["ASCII", "Unicode", "BCD", "Gray code", "EBCDIC"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Option 1: ASCII is a character encoding system that assigns numeric codes to and symbols used in text representation. ASCII It does not relate to minimizing errors in digital circuits or ensuring a single-bit change in transitions', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2074, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02075', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What will be the octal equivalent of 14 5 (base 5) ?', '["98", "168", "118", "188", "128"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Convert decimal 14 to octal: 14(10) = 14(10) = 16(8). This matches "118".', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2075, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02076', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What is the selection of capacities used to represent a feature in EBCDIC and BCD code systems respectively?', '["4 8 bits", "8 16 bits", "7 5 bits", "4 7 bits", "8 4 bits"]'::jsonb, 5, 'EBCDIC (Extended Binary Coded Decimal Interchange Code) EBCDIC is an 8-bit character encoding system. EBCDIC It can represent 256 characters (2⁸ = 256). th Mainly used in IBM mainframe and midrange systems', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2076, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
