('alict_02078', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'A magician writes a number in and he tells the audience that if they read it still means the same ixLHdxlfhka ,shk Tyq fm%alaIlhkag mjikafka Tjqka th miqmig tys w.h iudk njhs'' Which of the following decimal numbers will be equal to what he wrote in binary?', '["12", "18", "24", "27", "28"]'::jsonb, 4, 'The magician wrote a palindromic binary meaning the binary representation reads the same forward and backward. Let''s convert each decimal number given as answers into binary to find the match. fidhd', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2078, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02079', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Consider the two binary numbers and If OR Y and Y , what will be the values of A and B respectively?', '["01001110, 101100001", "10110001, 00000000", "10110001, 11111111", "11111111, 00000000", "11111111, 10110001"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Let''s find the values of A and B using the given values of X and Y . X = 101100012 Y = 010011102 A = X OR Y 1 0 1 0 1 OR 0 1 0 1 0 1 B = X AND Y 1 0 1 0 1 AND 0 1 0 1 0 So', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2079, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02080', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'A computer uses 8-bit signed numbers. What is the result of adding (-45) and (27) using two''s complement arithmetic?', '["11001010", "11001110", "01101010", "11101110", "10000000"]'::jsonb, 4, '• Step Convert to 8-bit two''s complement. 8 foflys Convert decimal -45 into binary 2 45 2 22 - 1 2 11 - 0 2 5 - 1 2 - 1 2 1 - 0 - 1 Get the 8-bit one''s complement by switching the zeros with ones because this is a negative number', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2080, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02081', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What will be the result of the bitwise XOR and bitwise AND operations between two binary numbers 111011002 and 010110012 respectively?', '["101101012, 010010002", "111111012, 010010002", "010010102, 111111012", "111100012, 010010012", "010010102, 010010002"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Step we need to perform the XOR operation on the binary numbers 111011002 and 010110012. XOR outputs 1 only when the two bits are different and 0 when they are the same', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2081, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
