('alict_02086', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Which of the following does not belong to BCD value?', '["1000", "1001", "0101", "1010", "0001"]'::jsonb, 4, 'BCD (Binary-Coded Decimal) represents decimal digits (0-9) using 4-bit binary values. Each group of 4 bits must correspond to a decimal digit from 0 (0000) to 9 (1001). BCD 4 lska Explanation of each option 1: 1000 is a valid BCD value. It represents decimal 8', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2086, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
