('alict_02088', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'In a 4-bit binary what happens when the sum exceeds 15 (1111₂)?', '["An overflow occurs", "The sum resets to zero", "The extra bits are ignored", "The sum is stored in a separate register", "No effect on the calculation"]'::jsonb, 1, 'In a 4-bit binary the maximum value that can be represented is 1111₂ (which is 15 in decimal). If the result of an addition exceeds this maximum it means the result requires more than 4 bits to represent it. 4 lg This condition is known as an overflow', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2088, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
