('alict_02358', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Which of the following best describes the purpose of the close() function in Python file handling?', '["It deletes the file after use. th", "It saves the file permanently and makes it read-only. th iqrlsk", "It flushes any unwritten data from the buffer and releases the file resource. th n*rfhka", "It reopens the file for reading after writing. th miq", "It automatically appends new data to the file. th iajhxl%Shj kj"]'::jsonb, 3, 'When you write to a Python may temporarily keep the data in a buffer Tn f.dkqjla ,shk close() makes sure this buffered data is flushed (written) to the actual file. close() n*rh It also releases the system resource so other programs or parts of your code can use the file safely', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2358, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
