('alict_02421', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Which of the following statements is true about functions in Python?', '["A function in Python must always return a value using the return statement", "Functions in Python can be defined inside other known as nested functions", "Python functions cannot accept multiple arguments", "Once a Python function cannot be called more than once", "A function''s variables defined inside the function are automatically global"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "Functions in Python can be defined inside other known as nested functions". Trace through the code line by line (variable assignments, loop iterations, and function calls) to confirm this result.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2421, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
