('alict_02423', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Which of the following Python list methods removes and returns an element of a list?', '["pop() This method removes the element at a given position in the list (default is the last element) and returns it. If no index is it will remove and return the last element. this method indeed fits the requirement of removing and returning the last element of a list", "remove() This method removes the first occurrence of a specified value from the list. It does not return the element and is not used to remove the last element", "clear() This method removes all elements from the making it empty. It does not return any so it doesn''t fit the requirement", "2", "1"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "pop() This method removes the element at a given position in the list (default is the last element) and returns it. If no index is it will remove and return the last element. this method indeed fits the requirement of removing and returning the last element of a list". Trace through the code line by line (variable assignments, loop iterations, and function calls) to confirm this result.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2423, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02424', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'What is the output of the python statement 10*2**3%7 ?', '["2", "3", "1", "5", "11 10 * 8 = 80. The modulo operator % returns the remainder of the division of the first operand by the second. 80 % 7 means dividing 80 by 7 and finding the remainder"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "3". Trace through the code line by line (variable assignments, loop iterations, and function calls) to confirm this result.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2424, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02425', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Which of the following statements about if-else conditions in Python is most accurate?', '["The else block is mandatory in an if-else statement. if-else", "Python supports the use of else without an accompanying if", "The elif keyword is used to handle multiple conditions in an if-else statement. elif moh if-else nyq fldkafoais", "You can only have one elif block in an if-else statement. if-else", "The colon (:) at the end of an if or else statement is optional in Python. if else wjidkfha"]'::jsonb, 3, 'In the elif keyword (short for "else if") allows you to handle multiple conditions within a single if-else statement. After an initial if you can use one or more elif blocks to check additional conditions', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2425, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
