('alict_02521', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'In each if x is its value is added to if x is its value is subtracted from y. After is decremented by 1, and th e loop repeats. The program effectively alternates between adding and subtracting the values of x as it counts down from 10 to 1. The sequence of operations results in y being updated as 10, 1, 9, 2, 8, 3, 7, 4, 6 and finally 5. when the loop completes and x reaches 0, the program outputs the final value of which is 5. Python x isg 10 olajd y isg 0 olajd miqj x 0 g ;dla Odjkh x tys w.h y g tys w.h y wvq fuhska miq" x 1 lska wvq ,nk Æmh jevigyk 10 isg 1 olajd .Kka x wvq y 10, 1, 9, 2, 7, 4, 6 wjidk 5'' Æmh x 0 5 y wjidk w.h the correct answer 2)', '["10", "5", "-10", "0", "5- 7"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "10". Trace through the code line by line (variable assignments, loop iterations, and function calls) to confirm this result.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2521, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
