('alict_02525', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'to the Python code snippet what is the correct relation for the id() function?', '["id(A) = id(E)", "id(A) = id(D)", "id(D) = id(E)", "id(A) = id(B) = id(C)", "id(C) = id(D)"]'::jsonb, 2, 'If you''re referring to the id() function in it returns the identity of an object. This can be useful for comparing whether two variables refer to the same object or not. Tn Python id() variables with the same value and same data type are stored in the same location in memory', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2525, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
