('alict_02527', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'is the output of the above Python code?', '["syntax error", "[3, 47, 62, 13, 25, 20]", "[3, 13, 20, 25, 47, 62]", "[62, 13, 25, 20, 3, 47]", "[62, 47, 25, 20, 13, 3]"]'::jsonb, 5, 'for i in range(3, 0, -1): print("*" * i) Here the For loop is used and the general format is this. for i in step): print(i) Accordingly and -1. starting from 3 and decreasing to , "*" will be output accordingly', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2527, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02528', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Which of the following is true about Python functions?', '["Functions in Python must always return a value using return", "The name parameter in the function is a keyword", "The greet function cannot be called without arguments. greet", "The print() statement returns the value to the caller. print()", "You cannot define functions inside other functions in Python. Tng"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: Incorrect - Python functions can return a value using but it''s not required. - Python Option 2: Incorrect - name is a not a keyword. - name Option 3: Correct - Since name has no default calling greet () without an argument will cause a', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2528, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02529', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Which PHP super global variable is used to access form data sent with the GET method? GET hjk ,o fmdaru PHP 3) Let''s consider each option one by one', '["$GLOBALS According to this it''s false. The $GLOBALS super global variable is used to access global variables from anywhere in the PHP not specifically for accessing form data sent with the GET method", "$_SERVER According to this it''s false. The $_SERVER super global variable contains information about and script but it is not used for accessing form data sent with the GET method", "$GLOBALS", "$_SERVER", "$_GET"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "$GLOBALS". Trace through the code line by line (variable assignments, loop iterations, and function calls) to confirm this result.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2529, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02530', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Fill in the blanks with the correct options regarding Python database connectivity in the correct order. Python iuqod lr we can connect to a database using the 1._________ module for or the sqlite3 module for SQLite. To execute SQL we first create a 2._________ object using the cursor() method. Queries are executed using the 3. _________ and to retrieve multiple rows from the result we use 4._________. After making changes to the we must call the 5._________ method to save them permanently. Python wmg 1._________ SQLite sqlite3 iuqodhlg SQL wms cursor() 2._________ 3. _________ nyq ,nd wms 4._________ iuqodhg miq" iq', '["cursor \u2192 mysql.connector \u2192 execute() \u2192 fetchall() \u2192 commit()", "execute() \u2192 fetchall() \u2192 cursor \u2192 mysql.connector \u2192 commit()", "mysql.connector \u2192 fetchall() \u2192 cursor \u2192 execute() \u2192 commit()", "mysql.connector \u2192 cursor \u2192 execute() \u2192 fetchall() \u2192 commit()", "cursor \u2192 execute() \u2192 mysql.connector \u2192 fetchall() \u2192 commit()"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Correct answer: "mysql.connector → cursor → execute() → fetchall() → commit()". Trace through the code line by line (variable assignments, loop iterations, and function calls) to confirm this result.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2530, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
