('alict_02533', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Which loop is most appropriate for iterating over the elements of an array in PHP?', '["For loop According to this it''s false. The for loop is commonly used for iterating over but it requires managing the index manually", "While loop According to this it''s false. The while loop can also be used for iterating over but it is less intuitive for this purpose as it also requires manual index handling", "Do...while loop According to this it''s false. The do...while loop is similar to the loop but ensures the loop runs at least once. It''s not typically the best choice for array iteration", "Foreach loop According to this it''s true. The foreach loop is designed specifically for iterating over arrays and is the most appropriate loop for this task in as it directly accesses each element without needing to manage the index manually", "Repeat loop According to this it''s false. There is no Repeat loop in so this option is incorrect"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "For loop According to this it''s false. The for loop is commonly used for iterating over but it requires managing the index manually". Trace through the code line by line (variable assignments, loop iterations, and function calls) to confirm this result.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2533, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
