('alict_02538', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Which of the following PHP statements correctly creates a connection in object -oriented style?', '["$conn = mysqli(\"localhost\", \"root\",", "$conn = new mysqli(\"localhost\", \"root\",", "$conn = connect_mysqli(\"localhost\", \"root\",", "$conn = mysqli_connect(\"localhost\", \"root\",", "$conn = db_connect(\"localhost\", \"root\","]'::jsonb, 2, 'In there are two main styles to connect to PHP Procedural style → uses functions like mysqli_connect(). Object-oriented style → uses the mysqli class with new. Option 1: Wrong. mysqli is a not a so you can''t call it like this', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2538, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
