('alict_02546', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'What is the purpose of $_SERVER[''PHP_SELF''] in PHP?', '["To return the name of the current server", "To list all server variables", "To output the current PHP script''s filename", "To close the current script", "To check if PHP is installed"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "To output the current PHP script''s filename". Trace through the code line by line (variable assignments, loop iterations, and function calls) to confirm this result.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2546, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02547', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Why does PHP use semicolons at the end of statements?', '["Semicolons are used to indicate the end of a PHP script. PHP script tll wjidkh Semicolons", "Semicolons improve code readability and maintainability. Semicolons", "Semicolons separate individual PHP allowing the interpreter to distinguish between them. Semicolons", "Semicolons are a requirement enforced by the PHP syntax. Semicolon", "Semicolons prevent syntax errors in PHP code. Semicolons PHP"]'::jsonb, 3, 'In semicolons act similarly to full stops at the conclusion of sentences. A semicolon marks the termination of one directive and the initiation of the subsequent one', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2547, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
