('alict_02550', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Given below are some Python codes. If a student wants to generate the output ''15'', which of the following Python codes is', '["A and B only", "B and C only", "A and C only", "All of the above", "None of the above"]'::jsonb, 3, '• Code A Above python code defines a recursive function named mystery. 1) If the input x is less than or equal to 0, the function returns 0. 0 g wvq iudk 2) If x is greater than 0, the function returns x plus the result of calling itself with Mystery(x-1)', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2550, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02551', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Which of the following is not a valid keyword in Python 3?', '["is", "raw_input", "global", "continue", "in"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "raw_input". Trace through the code line by line (variable assignments, loop iterations, and function calls) to confirm this result.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2551, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02552', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Which of the following statements about PHP is true?', '["PHP is a client-side scripting language used primarily for creating interactive web pages. PHP", "PHP code is executed on the client''s browser and can access the client''s local files. PHP", "PHP can be embedded within and is executed on the server -side to generate dynamic web pages. PHP\"", "PHP does not support database making it unsuitable for building data-driven websites. PHP", "PHP scripts are compiled into machine code before they are executed. PHP"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "PHP can be embedded within and is executed on the server -side to generate dynamic web pages. PHP"". Trace through the code line by line (variable assignments, loop iterations, and function calls) to confirm this result.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2552, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02553', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Which of the following statements about Python''s handling of variables and memory is true?', '["Python uses explicit memory requiring the programmer to manually allocate and deallocate memory", "In variables must be declared with their data type before they can be used", "Python uses a reference counting mechanism combined with garbage collection to manage memory", "Python variables are statically meaning their type is fixed at compile time", "Memory for Python variables is allocated on the stack"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "Python uses a reference counting mechanism combined with garbage collection to manage memory". Trace through the code line by line (variable assignments, loop iterations, and function calls) to confirm this result.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2553, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02554', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Which of the following is a property of Python dictionaries?', '["Dictionaries can have duplicate keys. Dictionary", "Keys in a dictionary must be mutable. Dictionary tll", "Dictionary values cannot be updated after they are assigned. Dictionary miq", "Dictionaries are unordered collections in Python versions prior to 3.7. Dictionary", "Dictionary keys must always be strings. Dictionary"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Option 1: This is False. Python dictionaries do not allow duplicate keys. If a duplicate key is the previous value for that key will be overwritten by the new value. Option 2: This is False. Dictionary keys must be immutable such as or tuples', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2554, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02555', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Which of the following is a major advantage of using COTS (Commercial Off-The-Shelf) software packages in an organization?', '["High customization options", "Lower upfront costs", "Faster implementation time", "Full control over the source code", "No need for external support"]'::jsonb, 3, 'One of the biggest advantages of COTS software is that it''s and ready for immediate use. This leads to much quicker implementation compared to custom-built which needs significant time for and deployment', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2555, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
