('alict_02558', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Which of the following conditions will return true in PHP?', '["if ($x)", "if (!$x)", "if ($x == true)", "if ($x true)", "if ($x != false)"]'::jsonb, 2, '1) if ($x) $x is so this is False. $x False ksid 2) if (!$x) !$x means NOT which is True. !$x lshkafka NOT False True 3) if ($x == true) $x == true → false == true → false', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2558, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02559', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Consider the following Python = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5] def = 0 for x in x % 2 == += x return total print(find_even_sum(sequence)) Which of the following is the output of this program?', '["6", "8", "10", "4", "12"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The program defines a list called sequence containing the numbers [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]. A function named find_even_sum(a) takes a list a as input and finds the sum of all even numbers in the list. jevigyk [1, 2, 3, 4, 5] wvx', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2559, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
