('alict_02563', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'PHP Which method should be used to securely handle form data that needs to be sent to server in PHP?', '["GET", "POST", "CONNECT", "DELETE", "UPDATE"]'::jsonb, 2, 'When handling form data in the POST method should be used for secure data transfer. This is because GET appends the data to the making it visible in the browser''s address bar and less secure', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2563, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02564', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Which of the following is true about embedding PHP code in an page?', '["PHP code must be placed within", "PHP code can only be embedded within the", "PHP code must be enclosed within", "PHP code is used only for client-side scripting PHP", "PHP code does not interact with databases PHP"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "PHP code must be enclosed within". Trace through the code line by line (variable assignments, loop iterations, and function calls) to confirm this result.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2564, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02565', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Which of the following PHP superglobals is used to collect form data after submitting an form with the POST method? POST fmdaruhla miq fmdaru', '["$_SESSION", "$_GET", "$_POST", "$_REQUEST", "$_COOKIE"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The correct answer is $_POST. In $_POST is a superglobal array specifically designed to collect data sent through an form using the POST method. When a form is submitted via the form''s data is sent securely in the request body rather than in the URL', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2565, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
