('alict_02567', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Why is extensive customization of COTS software often discouraged in large-scale enterprise projects?', '["It always makes the software free to use. th", "Customization increases maintenance complexity and breaks compatibility with vendor upgrades", "Customization is guaranteed to improve vendor support", "All vendors officially encourage deep modifications of source code", "It makes integration with other systems fully automatic. th"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: Incorrect. Customization doesn''t make software free. COTS software is paid ,nd Option 2: Correct. This is the main reason why customization is discouraged. Over -customizing makes it hard to and incompatible with future updates provided by the vendor', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2567, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02568', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'What will happen if a form with is but the PHP script tries to access the form data using $_GET?', '["The form data will still be accessible via $_GET. fmdaruh", "An error will be thrown because $_GET is not defined. $_GET", "The form data will not be accessible using and the script will not receive any submitted data. $_GET", "PHP will automatically convert the $_GET request into $_POST. PHP", "The form submission will and the browser will show an error message. fmdaruh"]'::jsonb, 3, 'In form data is sent to the server using either the GET or POST which determines how the data is transmitted and accessed. PHP fmdaru When is used in a the submitted data is stored in the $_POST superglobal array. fmdaruhl', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2568, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02569', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'What will be the output of this Python code?', '["7", "10", "5", "8", "11"]'::jsonb, 3, 'values for each variable had been given (for b and c). So we have to assign the values for the variables in the calculation assigned to the outcome. a + b * c // a - b % c 7 + 3 * 4 // 7 - 3 % 4 according to the operator we have to calculate the given calculation', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2569, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02570', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Which of the following is not a B2B (business-to-business) transaction?', '["A company purchasing raw materials from a supplier for manufacturing purposes. iud.ula", "An individual buying a laptop from an online retailer for personal use", "A software company licensing its product to another company for use in their business operations", "A marketing agency hiring a freelance graphic designer for a client project", "An organization outsourcing its payroll processing to a specialized payroll service provider"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "An individual buying a laptop from an online retailer for personal use". Trace through the code line by line (variable assignments, loop iterations, and function calls) to confirm this result.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2570, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02571', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Which function in PHP is used to return the length of a string?', '["strlen()", "strlength()", "len()", "string_length()", "str_len()"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The correct answer is 1) strlen(). Explanation In the strlen() function is specifically used to determine and return the length of a string. The syntax is strlen($string), where $string is the string variable whose length you want to calculate', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2571, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02572', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'def myfunc = a+2 a = a*2 return a print myfunc (2) What is the output of the above code?', '["8", "4", "16", "Indentation error", "0"]'::jsonb, 4, 'The lines inside the function are not indented. This will lead to an indentation error. The error occurs because Python expects the body of the function to be indented. Below is the corrected version of that def myfunc(a): a = a + 2 a = a * 2 return a print myfunc(2)', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2572, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02573', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Which of the following statements correctly describes language translators?', '["Interpreter has faster execution compared to other translators", "Interpreter converts entire source code into machine code", "Compiler has slower execution compared to other translators", "Interpreter detects errors during execution", "Compiler runs code line-by-line during program execution"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Correct answer: "Interpreter detects errors during execution". Trace through the code line by line (variable assignments, loop iterations, and function calls) to confirm this result.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2573, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
