('alict_02575', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Which PHP superglobal is used to collect form data sent with the "POST" method? "POST" hjk ,o', '["$_GET", "$_FORM", "$_POST", "$_REQUEST", "$_INPUT"]'::jsonb, 3, '1) $_GET This superglobal is used to collect data sent with the GET method. superglobal GET hjk 2) 2) $_FORM This is not a valid PHP superglobal. 3) $_POST This is the correct answer. It collects data sent with the POST method', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2575, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02576', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Consider the following Python = 5 def += 1 return n print(increment()) print(count) What will happen when this code is executed?', '["6", "6 5", "5 6", "5", "Error"]'::jsonb, 2, 'count = 5 → global variable. In the default value of n is set to the current value of count (5) at function definition time. n w.hg ilid Inside the n += 1 → n = 6. return n → prints 6. The global count is not so print(count) → 5', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2576, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02577', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'In constants offer a way to define values that remain unchanged throughout the execution of a script. Which of the following statements about PHP constants is correct?', '["Constants in PHP can be defined without using quotation marks for their values. PHP", "Constants can only be defined using the const keyword within classes", "Constants are automatically local and can only be accessed within the function where they are defined", "PHP constants allow for dynamic value assignment during runtime using the const() function. PHP", "Constants in PHP can be reassigned new values using the unset() function PHP"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "Constants in PHP can be defined without using quotation marks for their values. PHP". Trace through the code line by line (variable assignments, loop iterations, and function calls) to confirm this result.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2577, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02578', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Consider the following python is the output of the above python code when execute?', '["5, 51, 5", "50, 51, 52", "5, 51, 51", "5,", "5"]'::jsonb, 1, 'When this Python code is it produces the output the global variable i is set to 5. The first which is 5, followed by a comma. the varscope() function is called. Within this a new local variable i is defined and assigned the value 50', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2578, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02579', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'What will be the output of this PHP code?', '["11 & 11 12 & 12 11 & 11 10 & 10", "10 & 11 12 & 12 11 & 11 & 10", "10 & 11 & 11 10 & 11 9 & 9", "10 & 11 12 & 12 & 12 11 & 11", "11 & 11 12 & 12 11 & 11 & 11 Line Operation $x Output 1 $x = 10; 10 2 echo $x++; 10 & 11 3 echo 12 & 12 4 echo 11 & 11 5 echo $x--; 11 & 10 Here $x is a variable and 10 is substituted for it"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "10 & 11 12 & 12 11 & 11 & 10". Trace through the code line by line (variable assignments, loop iterations, and function calls) to confirm this result.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2579, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02580', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'What is main purpose of the mysqli_real_escape_string() function in a PHP database connection?', '["To establish a secure connection to the database", "To prevent SQL injection by escaping special characters in a string before using it in an SQL query. SQL", "To execute an SQL query and fetch results from the database. SQL", "To close an existing database connection", "To encrypt sensitive data before inserting it into the database"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The mysqli_real_escape_string() function is used to escape special characters in a string to prevent SQL injection attacks', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2580, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
