('alict_02582', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Which of the following statements is true about PHP?', '["PHP stands for Personal Home Page", "PHP is a server-side scripting language", "PHP can only run on Windows servers", "PHP is primarily used for client-side scripting. PHP", "PHP is a markup language similar to"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "PHP is a server-side scripting language". Trace through the code line by line (variable assignments, loop iterations, and function calls) to confirm this result.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2582, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02583', 10, 'Systems Analysis & Design', 'Which of the following statements about software development life cycle models is TRUE?', '["The Waterfall model allows easy iteration between phases during development", "Agile methodology emphasizes continuous collaboration and flexible responses to change. Agile", "The Spiral model does not involve risk analysis in its phases", "The V-Model skips testing phases until the final product is completed. wjidk wjika", "Prototyping model is best suited for projects with fixed and well-defined requirements. fyd\u00a2ka"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: This is false. Waterfall is a sequential approach where each phase must be completed before moving to the next. It doesn''t support easy going back or making it rigid when requirements change. iydh fkdolajk Option 2: This is true', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Systems Analysis & Design', NULL, 2583, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02584', 10, 'Systems Analysis & Design', 'In the Agile how is progress typically measured?', '["By the completion of phases", "By the number of defects found", "By working software increments", "By the number of requirements gathered", "By the amount of documentation created"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "By working software increments". This follows from standard systems-development lifecycle (SDLC) concepts.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Systems Analysis & Design', NULL, 2584, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02585', 10, 'Systems Analysis & Design', 'What system development model is appropriate for systems where the requirement is clear and consistent?', '["Waterfall model", "Spiral model", "Agile model", "Prototyping", "Rapid Application development"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "Waterfall model". This follows from standard systems-development lifecycle (SDLC) concepts.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Systems Analysis & Design', NULL, 2585, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02586', 10, 'Systems Analysis & Design', 'Which of the following is most widely used requirement gathering method in system development ixj¾Ok', '["Observation", "Questionnaire", "Interviews", "Collecting information from documents", "Engage in real work"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The given PHP code initializes $num to 10 and then calculates the expression ($num++ + ++$num ). $num++ (post-increment) evaluates to 10, using the current value before incrementing $num to 11. ++$num (pre-increment) increments $num to 12 and then evaluates to 12', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Systems Analysis & Design', NULL, 2586, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02587', 10, 'Systems Analysis & Design', 'In which of the following best describes the purpose and outcome of the Logical Data Modeling step within the Analysis phase?', '["To convert high -level business requirements into detailed system focusing on the hardware and software infrastructure required for implementation", "To create a detailed blueprint of the system''s physical data including file structures and indexing to ensure efficient data retrieval and storage", "To develop a conceptual model that represents the data structures and relationships in a manner independent of physical allowing for an abstract view of the data needs", "To perform a feasibility analysis that assesses the practicality of proposed solutions in terms of and technology constraints before proceeding to system design", "To evaluate the user interface design and interactions to ensure usability and accessibility requirements are met before the system is developed"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: Describes the purpose of the System Design phase rather than the Analysis phase. It involves defining detailed system specifications and infrastructure not data modeling', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Systems Analysis & Design', NULL, 2587, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02588', 10, 'Systems Analysis & Design', 'Among the following information system development the most popular development model', '["Spiral model", "Object model", "Waterfall model", "Incremental development model", "Rapid development model"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "Waterfall model". This follows from standard systems-development lifecycle (SDLC) concepts.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Systems Analysis & Design', NULL, 2588, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02589', 10, 'Systems Analysis & Design', 'A proposed hospital management system was found to be difficult for the hospital staff to adapt and it would disrupt their daily ld¾h wmyiq nj fidhd .kakd ,o th Tjqkaf.a ffoksl ld¾h jkq feasibility is most relevant here', '["Economic feasibility", "Operational feasibility", "Technical feasibility", "Schedule feasibility", "Legal feasibility"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Operational feasibility focuses on whether the system will work in including user workflow and practicality in daily operations', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Systems Analysis & Design', NULL, 2589, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02590', 10, 'Systems Analysis & Design', 'Which of the following is true about system testing', '["Each component of a system is inspected at the implementation phase", "Unit testing is conducted by project manager", "Acceptance testing is used to inspect whether each tested module is combined accurately. ,o", "Acceptance test is conducted by software development team only", "Integrated testing is performed by software development team including software engineers and project managers"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Correct answer: "Integrated testing is performed by software development team including software engineers and project managers". This follows from standard systems-development lifecycle (SDLC) concepts.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Systems Analysis & Design', NULL, 2590, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02591', 10, 'Systems Analysis & Design', 'What is the most popular development model of the following system development models?', '["Spiral model", "Object Oriented model", "Waterfall model", "Incremental Development model", "Rapid Development model"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Spiral model A risk-driven process model that combines elements of both iterative and waterfall models. It''s used for complex projects but isn''t as widely adopted as other models due to its complexity and cost', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Systems Analysis & Design', NULL, 2591, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02592', 10, 'Systems Analysis & Design', 'In a system development the purpose of the feasibility study is', '["Develop system requirements", "Design the technical architecture", "Determine the cost-effectiveness of the project", "Implement the system software", "Train users on the new system"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: While understanding the feasibility of a project can lead to discussions about system the primary purpose of a feasibility study is not to develop these requirements. This is typically done in later like requirements gathering', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Systems Analysis & Design', NULL, 2592, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02593', 10, 'Systems Analysis & Design', 'Which of the following is a key characteristic of the Waterfall model in the System Development Life Cycle', '["It allows for constant iteration and revisiting of previous stages. th", "It is highly flexible and adaptive to changes during development. th", "It follows a linear and sequential approach where each stage must be completed before moving to the next. th", "It is specifically designed for rapid prototyping and iterative development. th", "It is best suited for projects with high levels of uncertainty and risk"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The Waterfall model in the System Development Life Cycle is known for its linear and sequential approach', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Systems Analysis & Design', NULL, 2593, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02594', 10, 'Systems Analysis & Design', 'What is the pair of diagrams those are not used in Structured System Analysis and Design Methodology?', '["Document Flow Context diagram", "Context Logical Data model", "UML Use Case Diagram UML", "ER Activity Diagram", "Context Activity Diagram"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "UML Use Case Diagram UML". This follows from standard systems-development lifecycle (SDLC) concepts.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Systems Analysis & Design', NULL, 2594, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02595', 10, 'Systems Analysis & Design', 'Which of the following best defines technical feasibility in system development?', '["It assesses whether the existing and software can support the proposed system. th", "It evaluates whether the new system can be built within the allocated budget. fjka ,o whjeh", "It determines if the system can be legally implemented without violating regulations", "It checks if the system will be accepted by end-users and integrated into daily operations. th", "It measures the system''s long-term benefits compared to its cost. th"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Technical feasibility focuses on whether the technology required and technical expertise) is available and capable of supporting the new system. It ensures the project can actually be implemented with current tools and infrastructure before proceeding', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Systems Analysis & Design', NULL, 2595, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02596', 10, 'Systems Analysis & Design', 'In system assesses the willingness and ability of the users to support and use the proposed system is known', '["Operational feasibility", "Technical feasibility", "Economical feasibility", "Legal feasibility", "Schedule feasibility"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "Operational feasibility". This follows from standard systems-development lifecycle (SDLC) concepts.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Systems Analysis & Design', NULL, 2596, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02597', 8, 'Web Development', 'Which of the following correctly describes the behavior of the <br> tag?', '["It is a semantic tag that structures paragraphs in documents. th", "It creates a line break without adding any semantic meaning. th", "It inserts a visible horizontal rule in the document. th", "It is replaced by", "It adds spacing between two elements. th"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "It creates a line break without adding any semantic meaning. th". This follows from standard HTML/CSS behaviour for the tag or property in question.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Web Development', NULL, 2597, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02598', 8, 'Web Development', 'Which of the following is incorrect about descriptive lists?', '["<dl> is a descriptive list", "<dt> is a descriptive term", "<dd> is a descriptive data", "<dl> has no closing tag", "is the correct order"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Correct answer: "<dl> has no closing tag". This follows from standard HTML/CSS behaviour for the tag or property in question.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Web Development', NULL, 2598, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02599', 8, 'Web Development', 'What happens when you include multiple <source> elements inside a <picture> tag?', '["All sources are loaded simultaneously", "The browser selects the first compatible source based on media queries", "The browser randomly chooses a source", "Only the last <source> element is used", "The"]'::jsonb, 2, 'When multiple queries or type attributes of each such as screen or browser capabilities. jeks Wmdx.fha Example The correct answer is 2) The browser selects the first compatible source based on media queries Other options Option 1: Incorrect', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Web Development', NULL, 2599, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02600', 8, 'Web Development', 'What does the <meta> tag provide in an document?', '["Metadata about the such as author and description", "A way to link to external stylesheets", "A way to define the document''s title", "A placeholder for a navigation menu navigation fukqj ioyd imhhs", "A way to embed multimedia content"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Option 1: Correct. The encoding. Option 2: Incorrect. Linking external stylesheets is done using the stylesheets ine¢h Option 3: Incorrect. The title is defined in the <title> My Page < Option 4: Incorrect. The Option 5: Incorrect', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Web Development', NULL, 2600, 'A/L Past Paper Series')
